2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] To set up the Blackmagic Design Intensity Pro 4K on Arch Linux, you will need the proprietary
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Blackmagic Desktop Video drivers, which are maintained by the community in the Arch User Repository
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] (AUR).
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here is an overview of the steps required to get the card operational:
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Install Kernel Headers
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] The Blackmagic driver compiles a Dynamic Kernel Module Support (DKMS) module. You must have the
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] kernel headers installed for your active kernel before building the package:
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • For the default kernel: `linux-headers`
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • For the LTS kernel: `linux-lts-headers`
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • For any hardened or zen variants, choose the corresponding `-headers` package.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Install the Desktop Video Driver
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] The necessary drivers and utilities are packaged in the AUR under the name `desktopvideo`.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can build and install this using your preferred AUR helper (such as `paru` or `yay`) or by
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] cloning the repository from the AUR and building it manually with `makepkg`.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Optional packages in the AUR you may also find useful:
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `desktopvideo-gui`: Provides the Blackmagic Desktop Video Setup utility for adjusting
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] card inputs, outputs, and format settings via a graphical interface.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `media-express`: The official capture and playback application provided by Blackmagic
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Design.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Enable the Background Service
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] The hardware relies on a helper daemon to communicate with software. After installing the package:
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Enable and start the `DesktopVideoHelper.service` using `systemctl`.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Check Firmware Status
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] The Intensity Pro 4K often requires a firmware check or update after driver updates:
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Run the `BlackmagicFirmwareUpdater status` command to ensure the on-board firmware matches the
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] installed driver version.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If an update is required, the utility will prompt you to apply it and reboot the machine.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 5. Verify the Kernel Modules
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Ensure the `blackmagic` and `blackmagic-io` modules load successfully. You can verify this using
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] `lsmod`.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Once the service is active and the firmware is verified, the card should be immediately accessible
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] to applications such as OBS Studio, DaVinci Resolve, or FFmpeg.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Please let me know if you would like specific command examples, assistance configuring the DKMS
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] modules, or guidance for a particular capture application.
2026-09-04 04:22:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
