2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] Switching to the `desktopvideo` package is a good approach. It is the more conventional AUR
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] package for Blackmagic cards, maintained to include the full suite of user-space utilities (such as
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] `BlackmagicFirmwareUpdater` and configuration symlinks in `/usr/bin`).
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here are the steps to switch over cleanly:
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Remove the current package
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] To avoid file conflicts between the two builds, remove `decklink`:
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo pacman -R decklink
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Install Desktop Video
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] Install `desktopvideo` (and optionally `desktopvideo-gui` if you want the graphical setup tool):
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] yay -S desktopvideo desktopvideo-gui
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] During installation, DKMS will automatically rebuild the modules for your kernel (`7.2.2-arch1-1`).
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Start the service
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] Ensure the background daemon is enabled and running:
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo systemctl enable --now DesktopVideoHelper.service
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Verify the firmware
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] The updater binary should now be available directly in your standard path:
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] BlackmagicFirmwareUpdater status
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:30:50 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
