2026-09-04 04:31:49 [skid@archlinux] command line verify?
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.002 15.05KB 4.58s
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can verify the card directly from the command line using a few different tools:
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Check Device Nodes
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] The Blackmagic driver creates specific character device nodes. You can verify they exist and are
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] initialized:
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ls -la /dev/blackmagic*
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] You should see entries such as `/dev/blackmagic/io0` corresponding to the Intensity Pro 4K.
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Verify with FFmpeg
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you have `ffmpeg` installed with DeckLink support enabled (the default Arch package typically
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] includes this), you can list all detected Blackmagic input devices:
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ffmpeg -sources decklink
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Alternatively, you can test capturing a quick 5-second sample or checking the input stream details:
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ffmpeg -f decklink -list_formats 1 -i "Intensity Pro 4K"
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Check Kernel Diagnostic Output
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] To verify that the driver initialized the PCIe card without hardware errors, inspect the kernel
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ring buffer:
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] dmesg | grep -i blackmagic
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] This will show messages logged when the card was detected, including hardware initialization and
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] negotiated PCIe link speed.
2026-09-04 04:31:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
