2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.003 18.09KB 3.56s
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] The official Arch Linux `ffmpeg` binary is built without `--enable-decklink` (due to license
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] incompatibilities between FFmpeg's GPL and Blackmagic's SDK). Because of that, the command exited
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] without querying the device.
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] To verify the card via command line without compiling a custom FFmpeg, you have two reliable
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] options:
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Check the device nodes
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] Run:
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] ls -l /dev/blackmagic*
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] If the kernel drivers attached to the card correctly, you will see a character device such as
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/dev/blackmagic/io0`.
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Check the kernel initialization logs
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] Run:
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo dmesg | grep -i blackmagic
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] This will print the driver registration messages, identify the card as an Intensity Pro 4K, and
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] report if the PCIe link negotiated properly.
2026-09-04 04:32:42 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:23 [skid@archlinux] other options for ffmpeg
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.007 19.08KB 5.87s
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] To use FFmpeg with your Intensity Pro 4K, FFmpeg must be built with `--enable-decklink` and
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] `--enable-nonfree`. Because the DeckLink SDK license is incompatible with the GPL, distribution of
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] binaries with both enabled is restricted, which is why standard repository packages omit it.
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here are the main ways to obtain DeckLink support in FFmpeg on Arch Linux:
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 1: Install a DeckLink-enabled FFmpeg package from the AUR
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] Several packages in the AUR rebuild FFmpeg with extra flags enabled:
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `ffmpeg-decklink`: Specifically tailored to include DeckLink support alongside standard
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] FFmpeg dependencies.
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `ffmpeg-full`: A comprehensive build that enables nearly all supported hardware
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] acceleration and capture APIs, including DeckLink.
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can install either using `yay`:
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] yay -S ffmpeg-decklink
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Note: Building FFmpeg from source takes a significant amount of CPU time.)*
2026-09-04 04:33:30 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
