2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] How to use `bmdcapture`
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] The primary utility provided is `bmdcapture`. Unlike generic capture cards, Blackmagic hardware
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] requires the capture format (resolution and framerate mode) to match the incoming signal precisely.
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Query available cards and supported modes
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] Run `bmdcapture` with the `-h` flag to inspect available mode integers and identify your device:
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] bmdcapture -h
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] Look through the printed list for the mode corresponding to your input signal (for example,
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] `1080p59.94`, `1080p60`, or `720p60`). Each mode corresponds to a number (such as `-m 12`).
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Pipe into standard FFmpeg
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] Once you know your device index (usually `-C 0`) and the video mode number, you can stream raw
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] video to standard output and pipe it straight into `ffmpeg`.
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] For example, to capture raw video/audio and encode it to an MP4 file:
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] bmdcapture -C 0 -m <mode_number> -A 2 -V 3 -F nut -f /dev/stdout | ffmpeg -i - -c:v libx264 -preset fast -c:a aac output.mp4
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-C 0`: Selects the first Blackmagic device (Intensity Pro 4K).
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-m <mode_number>`: The video format detected from `-h`.
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-A 2`: Audio input selection (e.g., embedded HDMI audio or analog RCA).
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-V 3`: Video input format (e.g., HDMI or Component).
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-F nut -f /dev/stdout`: Encapsulates the uncompressed stream in a lightweight container suitable
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] for piping to standard output.
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `ffmpeg -i -`: Instructs FFmpeg to read the piped stream from standard input.
2026-09-04 04:34:51 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
