2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 1: Use `media-express` command-line / SDK samples
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] Since you have the `decklink` package installed, the official DeckLink SDK sample applications are
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] usually available. The SDK includes a ready-made command-line utility called `Capture` (or
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] `CapturePreview`):
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can check if the sample binaries were compiled and installed on your system:
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] find /usr -name "Capture" 2>/dev/null
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] If present, this utility can capture uncompressed YUV directly from the card to `stdout`.
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:35:16 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
