2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.008 25.04KB 5.84s
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] Yes, running `make` is almost the entire build process, but it requires two details to succeed
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] cleanly:
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Build Dependencies
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `bmdtools` uses FFmpeg’s internal libraries to mux the captured video into a stream format. Ensure
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] you have the standard build utilities and `pkg-config` available:
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo pacman -S --needed base-devel
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Your system `ffmpeg` package already provides the required library headers).*
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. DeckLink SDK Path
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `bmdtools` needs to know where the Blackmagic SDK header files are located.
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] Depending on how the `decklink` AUR package installed them, they are typically either in
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/usr/include` or `/usr/include/decklink`.
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can check their location with:
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] ls /usr/include | grep -i decklink
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If headers are directly in `/usr/include`:
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   git clone https://github.com/lu-zero/bmdtools.git
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   cd bmdtools
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   make
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If headers are in `/usr/include/decklink`:
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   git clone https://github.com/lu-zero/bmdtools.git
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   cd bmdtools
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]   make SDK_PATH=/usr/include/decklink
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] Once compilation completes (usually only a few seconds), the `bmdcapture` binary will appear in the
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] directory. You can test it immediately by running `./bmdcapture -h`.
2026-09-04 04:37:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
