2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] The Makefile defaults to a relative SDK path (`../../include/DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp`), which
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] expects the repository to sit directly inside a DeckLink SDK tree.
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] To compile it using the SDK files installed on your system, you need to point `SDK_PATH` to where
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] the package placed `DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp`.
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] First, locate the file on your system:
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] find /usr -name "DeckLinkAPIDispatch.cpp" 2>/dev/null
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] Once you have the directory containing that file (for example, `/usr/include` or
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/usr/src/decklink-...`), pass it to `make` via the `SDK_PATH` variable:
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] make SDK_PATH=/path/to/directory
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] If the `find` command returns no results, let me know where the `decklink` package installed its
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] files:
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-04 04:38:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] pacman -Ql decklink | grep -i decklinkapi
