2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here is how the flow can be structured:
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Execution Mechanism
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] In modern Deno, `Deno.Command` is the standard way to run system processes.
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Determine the shell by platform:
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Linux / macOS: Run `sh` or `bash` with `["-c", commandString]`.
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Windows: Run `cmd.exe` with `["/c", commandString]` or `powershell.exe` with
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] `["-Command", commandString]`.
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • I/O Handling:
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * If you want direct interactive execution (preserving colors, cursor controls, and streaming
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] directly to the terminal), set `stdin`, `stdout`, and `stderr` to `"inherit"`.
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * If you instead want the shell output captured into `relay`'s conversation history or
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] `outputBuffer`, set `stdout: "piped"` and read the resulting output buffer with `TextDecoder`.
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Integration Points in `relay.ts`
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Dedicated Handler Function:
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash]   Create a reusable named function (e.g., `executeShellCommand(commandLine: string)`) that parses
2026-09-05 07:13:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] the command and manages process spawning and error handling.
