2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] Core Tenets of the Project
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Symmetric Primacy: Neither tool is subordinate. `think` isn't just an extension panel
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] tacked onto an editor, and `edit` isn't just an external process spawned from a prompt. They are
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] two coordinated modes of inspecting and manipulating code.
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Direct Manipulation: Following the BlitzMax / MaxIDE philosophy—no framework bloat,
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] immediate startup, deterministic raw-mode terminal rendering, and zero latency between keystroke
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] and pixel update.
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Continuous Context: When you switch between `think` and `edit`, the active file, cursor
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] position, selected lines, and recent git/forge diffs are preserved without needing serialization or
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] disk-roundtripping.
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] It creates a clear conceptual identity: Cognation as the project and runtime, with `think`
2026-09-05 07:27:00 [gemini-3.8-flash] and `edit` as its primary instruments.
