2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.047 190.5KB 5.60s
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] To install a Deno-based project cleanly on Arch Linux, there are three common approaches depending
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] on whether you want a compiled native binary, a Deno script runner, or a user-local shell wrapper.
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. `deno compile` (Single Self-Contained Binary)
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] This generates an ELF binary with the Deno runtime and your dependencies bundled inside. It has
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] zero external dependencies on the target machine and starts instantly.
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Compile the entry point:
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] deno compile --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-net --allow-run -o cog main.ts
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Install to standard user bin:
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] install -Dm755 cog ~/.local/bin/cog
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Ensure `~/.local/bin` is in your `$PATH` via `~/.bashrc` or `~/.zshrc`)*.
2026-09-05 07:32:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. `deno install` (Managed Script Launcher)
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] `deno install` symlinks or creates a wrapper executable inside `$DENO_INSTALL_ROOT/bin` (or
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] `~/.deno/bin`).
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] deno install --global --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-net --allow-run -n cog main.ts
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] To make it available globally across the system:
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo env "PATH=$PATH" deno install --root /usr/local --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-net --allow-run -n cog main.ts
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Local Development Symlink / Wrapper (Best for Iteration)
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you are actively modifying the TypeScript source and want changes reflected immediately without
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] recompiling:
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Create an executable shell wrapper (e.g. `~/.local/bin/cog`):
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] #!/usr/bin/env bash
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] exec deno run --allow-read --allow-write --allow-env --allow-net --allow-run "/path/to/cog/main.ts" "$@"
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Make it executable:
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] chmod +x ~/.local/bin/cog
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Verification
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Check if anything on your Arch system already claims the name:
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] which cog
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] pacman -Qo $(which cog 2>/dev/null) 2>/dev/null
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] If `which cog` returns empty, your local path has full ownership of the command.
2026-09-05 07:32:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
