2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.048 199.5KB 6.98s
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] In this current conversation, no tools have been invoked yet, so there are no tool call results in
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] our session context.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you mean within `relay.ts` itself: yes.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] When a model invokes a function, `relay.ts` processes the call and stores the result in
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `rohaHistory`:
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. `processToolCalls()` executes the requested function (such as `read_time`, `submit_file`,
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `fetch_file`, or `tag_slop`).
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. An entry with `role: "tool"`, `tool_call_id`, `name`, and the returned `content` is pushed into
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] `rohaHistory`.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. In subsequent turns (and in recursive turns within `relay()`), those entries are serialized and
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] returned to the model:
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]    - For Google / Gemini: formatted as `role: "function"` with a `functionResponse` part.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]    - For OpenAI / DeepSeek: formatted as standard `role: "tool"` messages linked to `tool_call_id`.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash]    - For Anthropic: mapped to corresponding tool result blocks.
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] As long as history is not reset (`/reset`) or stripped, the model retains full visibility into
2026-09-05 07:40:48 [gemini-3.8-flash] previous tool results.
