2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.050 206.1KB 6.04s
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] On Arch Linux, you cannot directly install Debian packages (`.deb`) using `pacman`. You have a few
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] clean, native ways to install the software instead:
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Check the Official Repositories & AUR First (Recommended)
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] Most software distributed as `.deb` is already packaged for Arch in the official repositories or
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] the Arch User Repository (AUR).
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] Search for the package:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] # Search official repos
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] pacman -Ss <app-name>
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] # Or search the AUR (if you use an AUR helper like yay or paru)
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] yay -Ss <app-name>
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] # or
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] paru -Ss <app-name>
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. If You Use VS Code Specifically
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] If that download prompt was for the official Microsoft VS Code `.deb`:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Official Microsoft build (from AUR):
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]   yay -S visual-studio-code-bin
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Open-source upstream build (official Arch extra repo):
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]   sudo pacman -S code
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. If You Must Extract / Repackage the `.deb` File
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] If the software is proprietary and only distributed as a `.deb` file with no AUR build available:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option A: Use `debtap` (Converts `.deb` to an Arch `pacman` package)
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Install `debtap` from the AUR:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]    yay -S debtap
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Update the debtap database (first run only):
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo debtap -u
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Convert the package:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]    debtap package_name.deb
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Install the resulting `.pkg.tar.zst` file with `pacman`:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo pacman -U package_name.pkg.tar.zst
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option B: Manual Extraction (No root / isolated inspection)
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] A `.deb` file is just an `ar` archive containing `data.tar.*`:
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] # Extract the contents using bsdtar (built into Arch)
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] bsdtar -xf package_name.deb
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] # Extract data.tar.* into a local folder
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] tar -xf data.tar.*
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] This leaves you with `usr/bin`, `usr/share`, etc., which you can inspect or run locally without
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] installing system-wide.
2026-09-05 07:46:38 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
