2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] That happens because VS Code’s built-in updater doesn't know how to update itself on Arch; it
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] assumes you're on Ubuntu/Debian and dumps you on the `.deb` download page.
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] On Arch, package updates should always go through your package manager (`pacman` or your AUR
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] helper).
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Update It via the Terminal
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] Check how it was installed:
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If you installed the official binary via the AUR (`visual-studio-code-bin`):
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   yay -Syu visual-studio-code-bin
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   # or with paru:
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   paru -Syu visual-studio-code-bin
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If you are using Arch’s open-source `code` package:
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   sudo pacman -Syu code
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Disable VS Code's Nag Screen
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] To stop VS Code from redirecting you to web downloads or popping up update notices that don't work
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] on Arch:
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Open settings in VS Code (`Ctrl+,`).
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Search for: `update.mode`
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Set Update: Mode to `none` (or `"manual"`).
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] Or add this directly to your `settings.json`:
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] "update.mode": "none"
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] This lets `pacman` or `yay` manage the updates cleanly without VS Code prompting you to download
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] `.deb` files.
2026-09-05 07:47:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
