2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] That is a common and convenient workflow on macOS. Typically, people achieve this by either:
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Using `deno install`, which compiles or packages the script reference into a small
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] executable stub located directly in `~/.deno/bin` (or another designated directory included in your
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] `$PATH`).
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Using shebang lines (`#!/usr/bin/env -S deno run ...`) directly inside executable
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] scripts placed in a custom directory on your `$PATH`.
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Using wrapper shell scripts or symlinks in a custom directory (such as `~/.local/bin` or
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/usr/local/bin`).
2026-09-05 08:14:39 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
