2026-09-05 08:14:59 [skid@archlinux] on arch what are my options for pathed script folders?
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.000 1.515KB 3.65s
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] On Arch Linux, the conventions adhere closely to the XDG Base Directory specification and the
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] Filesystem Hierarchy Standard (FHS). Here are the primary options depending on whether you want the
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] scripts accessible to a single user or system-wide:
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. User-Specific Locations (Recommended)
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] These directories do not require root privileges (`sudo`) to add or edit scripts, keeping your
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] personal workflow clean and isolated.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `~/.local/bin`
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Status: The modern standard (XDG-compliant).
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Behavior: Systemd-based user sessions and many desktop environments automatically
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] append this directory to `$PATH` if it exists when you log in. If not already present, you can add
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] it to your shell configuration (`~/.bashrc`, `~/.zshrc`, etc.).
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Best for: General user scripts, Python user installs (`pip install --user`), and
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] standard user-level binaries.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `~/bin`
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Status: Traditional Unix convention.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Behavior: Historically popular and often supported out-of-the-box by default shell
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] skeleton files (`/etc/skel/.bashrc`).
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Best for: Personal preference if you prefer fewer subdirectories in your home folder.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `~/.deno/bin`
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Status: Deno-specific standard.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Behavior: Default installation target when running `deno install`.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Best for: Isolating Deno-managed executables. You can either export this directly into
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] your `$PATH` or keep your general scripts in `~/.local/bin` and symlink into it.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. System-Wide Locations
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] These directories apply to every user account on the machine and require root permissions to manage
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] files.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `/usr/local/bin`
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Status: Standard system administrator hierarchy (FHS).
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Behavior: Pre-configured in `$PATH` on practically all Arch Linux installations.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Best for: Custom tools, compiled utilities, or team-shared scripts meant for all users
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] without conflicting with Arch's package manager (`pacman`).
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `/usr/bin`
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Status: Managed strictly by `pacman`.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Recommendation: Avoid placing custom scripts here directly, as package upgrades or name
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] collisions could cause issues or overwrite files.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] Recommendation
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] For Deno scripts and local utility shortcuts on Arch, `~/.local/bin` (or
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] `~/.deno/bin` if relying heavily on `deno install`) offers the smoothest integration with
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] contemporary Linux tooling.
2026-09-05 08:15:03 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
