2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Looking at your current `$PATH`, neither `~/.local/bin` nor `~/.deno/bin` is currently included.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here are your best options to proceed on Arch:
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 1: Use `/usr/local/bin` (Immediately available)
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/usr/local/bin` is already in your `$PATH`.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Pros: Works right away without modifying shell configuration files.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Cons: Requires `sudo` to add, edit, or remove scripts, and targets the whole system
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] rather than just your user account.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 2: Add `~/.local/bin` (Recommended for personal scripts)
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] This aligns with modern Linux standards and does not require root privileges.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] To enable it, append the following line to your shell configuration file (e.g., `~/.bashrc` if
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] using Bash, or `~/.zshrc` if using Zsh):
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] After updating the file, apply the change with `source ~/.bashrc` (or `source ~/.zshrc`), or simply
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] open a new terminal session.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 3: Add `~/.deno/bin`
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you use `deno install` to automatically generate executable wrappers, Deno defaults to putting
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] them into `~/.deno/bin`.
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can append that directly to your shell profile as well:
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] export PATH="$HOME/.deno/bin:$PATH"
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:17:53 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (You can also combine them, e.g.: `export PATH="HOME/.local/bin:HOME/.deno/bin:$PATH"`).*
