2026-09-05 08:23:52 [skid@archlinux] is curate a valid title or credit in a repo
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.004 513B 5.53s
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] Yes, it is valid and increasingly common, particularly in data-centric, research, and
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] resource-aggregation repositories.
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] Here is how and where it is typically applied:
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Research and Dataset Repositories
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • CRediT Taxonomy: In academic and research repositories (e.g., Zenodo, Figshare, Dryad),
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] contributor roles often follow the CRediT (Contributor Roles Taxonomy) standard. One of the
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 14 official roles is "Data Curation", which encompasses managing, annotating, cleaning, and
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] maintaining research data.
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Citation File Format (`CITATION.cff`): When preparing citation metadata for repositories
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] containing data or software, curation roles are frequently specified in author and contributor
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] metadata.
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Hugging Face / Machine Learning: Repositories hosting datasets, model collections, or
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] benchmarks routinely credit contributors as "Data Curators" or "Dataset Curators".
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Open-Source Resource Lists ("Awesome" Lists)
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Repositories that aggregate tools, libraries, or articles (such as GitHub "Awesome" lists) often
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] credit maintainers and major contributors as "Curators" or note "Curated by
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] [Name]", rather than traditional software engineering titles like "Developer" or "Author".
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Open-Source Contributor Frameworks
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • All Contributors Specification: While the default emoji key uses categories like `data`
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] or `content`, projects frequently adapt these definitions to credit curation work explicitly in
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] `README.md` contributor tables.
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] Phrasing Recommendation
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] For clarity and consistency with standard contributor conventions, noun or participle forms are
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] generally preferred over the base verb:
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Role title: "Curator", "Data Curator", or "Content Curator"
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Attribution line: "Curated by [Name]" or "Curation: [Name]"
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Category tag: "Data Curation" or "Curation"
2026-09-05 08:23:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.011 28.53KB 8.50s
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] Several notable entries and differences stand out compared to current stable Godot releases (such
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] as 4.3 / 4.4):
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Expanded Skeleton & Procedural Animation Nodes
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] A substantial suite of new 3D procedural animation and inverse kinematics modifiers is present:
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • IK Solvers & Modifiers: `CCDIK3D`, `ChainIK3D`, `FABRIK3D`, `IterateIK3D`,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] `JacobianIK3D`, `SplineIK3D`, `TwoBoneIK3D`, `AimModifier3D`, `LookAtModifier3D`,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] `RetargetModifier3D`, `ConvertTransformModifier3D`, and `CopyTransformModifier3D`.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Bone Restraints & Utilities: `BoneTwistDisperser3D`, `ModifierBoneTarget3D`,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] `LimitAngularVelocityModifier3D`, `JointLimitation3D`, and `JointLimitationCone3D`.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Spring Bone Simulation: A dedicated spring bone suite, including `SpringBoneSimulator3D`
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] alongside capsule, plane, and sphere collision shapes (`SpringBoneCollision*`).
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. OpenXR Spatial & Entity Extensions
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] Extensive OpenXR tracking and spatial anchoring APIs are declared:
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Spatial capability configurations for markers (AprilTag, ArUco, QR code, Micro QR code), planes,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] and anchors.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Fine-grained spatial component containers (`OpenXRSpatialComponent*` for bounds, meshes,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] parentage, alignment, and persistence).
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Editor integration tools such as `OpenXRInteractionProfileEditor` and
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] `OpenXRBindingModifierEditor`.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Editor & UI Additions
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `EditorToaster`: Editor toast notification management.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `FoldableContainer` & `FoldableGroup`: Collapsible container structures.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `BlitMaterial` & `ColorPalette`: Dedicated resources for blitting and palette management.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Recent 4.3 additions are also represented, including `TileMapLayer` and `StatusIndicator`.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Format & Syntax Notes
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • The file structure uses JSON keys but specifies list elements as raw identifiers rather than
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] quoted strings.
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] • There is a syntax mismatch at the `"globals"` field, which opens with `{` but closes with `]`,
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] and missing commas between some high-level keys (e.g., after `"variant"`).
2026-09-05 08:25:57 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
