2026-09-05 13:40:16 [skid@archlinux] arch godot flatpack headless examples
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.2 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.006 507B 5.79s
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] When running Godot headlessly through Flatpak on Arch Linux, the primary tool is the `flatpak run`
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] command paired with Godot's `--headless` argument (Godot 4) or `--no-window` argument (Godot 3).
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Because Flatpak runs applications inside a sandbox, you will often need to grant filesystem
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] permissions (such as `--filesystem=host` or granting access to the current working directory) so
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Godot can read project files and write export outputs.
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Prerequisites on Arch Linux
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Ensure Flatpak is installed and the Godot package is present:
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo pacman -S flatpak
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak install flathub org.godotengine.Godot
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Common Headless Usage Examples
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Running a Project Headlessly
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] To launch a project as a dedicated server or without opening an X11/Wayland window:
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak run --filesystem=host org.godotengine.Godot --headless --path /path/to/your/project
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Running a Standalone Script Headlessly
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] To execute an entry-point script (such as a database migration, maintenance task, or test suite)
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] and exit:
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak run --filesystem=host org.godotengine.Godot --headless --path /path/to/your/project -s res://path/to/script.gd
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Headless Project Export
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] To build and export a release or debug binary headlessly (for CI/CD pipelines or local automation):
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Export Release:*
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak run --filesystem=host org.godotengine.Godot --headless --path /path/to/your/project --export-release "Linux/X11" /path/to/output/game.x86_64
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Export Debug:*
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak run --filesystem=host org.godotengine.Godot --headless --path /path/to/your/project --export-debug "Linux/X11" /path/to/output/game_debug.x86_64
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Note:* Ensure the export preset name (e.g., `"Linux/X11"` or `"Linux"`) matches the preset
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] configured in your project's `export_presets.cfg`.
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Importing Assets in Batch Mode
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] To trigger asset re-importing in a newly cloned project before building:
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] flatpak run --filesystem=host org.godotengine.Godot --headless --path /path/to/your/project --editor --quit
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] Useful Flags Reference
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] ╭──────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-05 13:40:22 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  Flag            │  Description                                                       │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ├──────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  :---            │  :---                                                              │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  `--headless`    │  Disables display, audio, and windowing subsystems (Godot 4+).     │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  `--path <dir>`  │  Specifies the directory containing `project.godot`.               │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  `-s <script>`   │  Runs a specific script inheriting `SceneTree` or `MainLoop`.      │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  `--quit`        │  Closes the engine immediately after the initial processing step.  │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] │  `--verbose`     │  Outputs detailed engine logs to standard output.                  │
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ╰──────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you would like example GDScript files tailored for headless execution or dedicated server
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] lifecycle management, please let me know.
2026-09-05 13:40:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.004 14.18KB 13.95s
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] I decoded the GDScript and cross-read it against the ClassDB reference. Here's my commentary.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] • What `scrape.gd` does*
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] A headless `SceneTree` bootstrap (`_init` → export → `quit`) that walks `ClassDB.get_class_list()`,
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] buckets every class into `node` / `resource` / `object` / `editor`, collects Variant type names,
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] and writes a tab-indented JSON "engine schema" (`res://godot_api_schema.json`) carrying package
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] metadata for the `nitrologic/biblispec` repo.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] • New / different vs. the ClassDB doc*
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] - The doc is stock Godot `ClassDB` API reference — nothing custom.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] - The script's categorization logic is the only non-standard part, and it maps cleanly onto
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] documented methods, so it's consistent with the reference.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] • Issues worth fixing*
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 1. `print_err(...)` in the failure branch of `export_engine_schema` is not a Godot function. There
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] is no such global; the correct calls are `printerr()` (stderr print) or `push_error()`. Because
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] GDScript resolves globals at compile time, this is a hard parse/compile error, so the script will
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] fail to load entirely — not just on the error path. This is the most important finding.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 2. The `object` bucket is effectively the full class list. Every engine class ultimately inherits
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] `Object`, so `ClassDB.is_parent_class(current_name, "Object")` is true for all of them. That's
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] presumably intentional as a catch-all, but it means `object` duplicates `ClassDB.get_class_list()`
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] and is not a meaningful partition alongside `node`/`resource`.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 3. `is_editor_class` uses a name-prefix heuristic (`"Editor"`, `"ResourceImporter"`). The reference
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] exposes a purpose-built alternative: `ClassDB.class_get_api_type()` returning `API_EDITOR` /
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] `API_EDITOR_EXTENSION`. That would also catch editor extension classes the prefix test
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] misses, and avoid false positives on non-editor classes that merely start with "Editor".
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 4. `get_variant_names` starts at `range(1, TYPE_MAX)`, skipping `TYPE_NIL` (0). `"Variant"` is
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] prepended manually and the `names.has()` guard dedupes it when the loop reaches `TYPE_VARIANT`, so
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] no duplicate — but "Nil" is silently dropped. Worth deciding deliberately.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 5. `ClassDB.get_class_list()` returns all classes regardless of enablement. If the schema should
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] reflect a runnable build, `ClassDB.is_class_enabled()` is available to filter.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] • Minor*
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] - Sorting each bucket after population is fine and deterministic.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] - Version string assembly and the metadata block look correct; no `Engine.get_version_info()` key
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] issues.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] If you want, I can sketch a corrected `export_engine_schema` using `class_get_api_type` and
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] `printerr` — say the word and I'll post it.
2026-09-13 09:25:37 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:33 [skid@archlinux] in godot can i get F12 key to toggle fullscreen and windowed mode?
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.002 17.09KB 7.08s
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] Yes. There's no built-in binding, but it's a few lines. Which API you use depends on the Godot
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] version.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] • Godot 4* — `DisplayServer.window_set_mode()`:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] extends Node
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] const FULLSCREEN_MODES := [
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN,
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN,
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] ]
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	if event is InputEventKey and event.pressed and not event.echo and event.keycode == KEY_F12:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 		toggle_fullscreen()
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 		get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] func toggle_fullscreen() -> void:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	var current_mode := DisplayServer.window_get_mode()
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	var is_fullscreen := current_mode in FULLSCREEN_MODES
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	var next_mode := DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_WINDOWED if is_fullscreen \
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 			else DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.window_set_mode(next_mode)
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] • Godot 3* — `OS.window_fullscreen`:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 	if event is InputEventKey and event.pressed and not event.echo and event.scancode == KEY_F12:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 		OS.window_fullscreen = not OS.window_fullscreen
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 		get_tree().set_input_as_handled()
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] Notes worth knowing:
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] - Rebindable alternative. Add an action (`toggle_fullscreen`) in Project Settings → Input
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] Map, bind F12 to it, then test `event.is_action_pressed("toggle_fullscreen")` instead of the raw
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] keycode. Cleaner if you ever expose rebinding.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] - `WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN` vs `EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN`. The former is borderless fullscreen
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] (better for alt-tab and multi-monitor); the latter grabs the display exclusively. If you only want
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] the borderless kind, drop the exclusive entry from the check.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] - macOS caveat. F12 is bound to Dashboard/Mission Control by default at the OS level, so
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] the key may never reach the window unless the user disables that shortcut. Many laptops also
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] require holding Fn.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] - Window focus. The key only arrives if the game window has focus; when running from the
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] editor the running window, not the editor, must be focused.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] - `set_input_as_handled()` prevents the event from also reaching `_input`/UI nodes.
2026-09-13 09:30:41 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:51 [skid@archlinux] so why not include set_input_as_handled???
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.001 19.44KB 3.06s
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] It is there — in both snippets. Let me point at the lines:
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] - Godot 4: `get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()` is the last line inside the `if` block.
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] - Godot 3: `get_tree().set_input_as_handled()` is the last line inside the `if`.
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] So neither example omits it. The only place it doesn't appear is the "Rebindable
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] alternative" bullet, where I described the change in prose rather than pasting full code. That was
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] just to keep the note short — the call belongs there too:
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 	if event.is_action_pressed("toggle_fullscreen"):
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 		toggle_fullscreen()
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 		get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] One clarification on why it matters, in case that's the underlying question: `_unhandled_input`
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] runs after `_input` and after the UI/`Control` nodes have had their chance, so by the time
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] your handler sees the event it's already "unclaimed." Marking it handled stops it from being passed
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] on to anything listening later in the same frame (other `_unhandled_input` handlers,
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] `_unhandled_key_input`), and keeps a keypress from also being consumed by the viewport's own
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] shortcuts. If you never mark it, the toggle still works — you just risk double-processing if more
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] than one node watches F12.
2026-09-13 09:31:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:31:56 [deepseek-flash] If you meant something different — e.g. you don't see it working, or it's missing in your
2026-09-13 09:31:56 [deepseek-flash] version of the code — paste that and I'll look.
