2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.002 21.09KB 4.85s
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] Fair enough — that's the chained `get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()`. Splitting it into a named
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] helper and a local keeps each statement a single call. Same for the key test and the mode
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] resolution.
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] • Godot 4*
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] extends Node
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] const FULLSCREEN_MODES := [
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN,
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_EXCLUSIVE_FULLSCREEN,
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] ]
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func _unhandled_input(event: InputEvent) -> void:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	if is_fullscreen_toggle_event(event):
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		toggle_fullscreen()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		mark_input_handled()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func is_fullscreen_toggle_event(event: InputEvent) -> bool:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	if not event is InputEventKey:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		return false
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	if not event.pressed:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		return false
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	if event.echo:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		return false
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	return event.keycode == KEY_F12
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func mark_input_handled() -> void:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	var viewport := get_viewport()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	viewport.set_input_as_handled()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func toggle_fullscreen() -> void:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	var current_mode := DisplayServer.window_get_mode()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	var next_mode := resolve_next_window_mode(current_mode)
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	DisplayServer.window_set_mode(next_mode)
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func resolve_next_window_mode(current_mode: int) -> int:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	if is_fullscreen_mode(current_mode):
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 		return DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_WINDOWED
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	return DisplayServer.WINDOW_MODE_FULLSCREEN
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func is_fullscreen_mode(mode: int) -> bool:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	return mode in FULLSCREEN_MODES
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] • Godot 3* — same shape, different API surface:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func mark_input_handled() -> void:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	var tree := get_tree()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	tree.set_input_as_handled()
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] func toggle_fullscreen() -> void:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	var is_fullscreen := OS.window_fullscreen
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 	OS.window_fullscreen = not is_fullscreen
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] Notes:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] - `event.keycode == KEY_F12` and `mode in FULLSCREEN_MODES` stay inline on purpose — those are
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] comparisons, not calls. Only calls get hoisted into helpers.
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] - `mark_input_handled` reads a bit oddly as a one-liner, but it keeps the call chain out of
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] `_unhandled_input` and gives you one place to change if you ever swap the viewport/tree.
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] - If you'd rather not have a function that just wraps two lines, the alternative is a single local:
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] `var viewport := get_viewport()` then `viewport.set_input_as_handled()`. Same effect, no extra
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] function. Your call which you prefer.
2026-09-13 09:32:21 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:32:40 [skid@archlinux] doe if return need to be sep lines?
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.009 23.53KB 33.87s
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] No — GDScript doesn't force that. A single statement after the colon is legal, so your guard
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] clauses can be one-liners:
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] func is_fullscreen_toggle_event(event: InputEvent) -> bool:
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 	if not event is InputEventKey: return false
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 	if not event.pressed: return false
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 	if event.echo: return false
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 	return event.keycode == KEY_F12
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] Three caveats:
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] - One statement only. `if x: return false` is fine; `if x: return false` plus anything else
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] on that line is not.
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] - `else` needs its own line. `if a: b` is allowed, but you can't chain `if a: b else: c` on
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] one line — the `else:` starts a new line.
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] - The style guide still prefers block form, so this is legal-but-discouraged. If your Godot
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] build ever complains, the block form is always safe.
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] What you can't do is put a function's body on the same line as its `func` header — this is
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] invalid:
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] func is_fullscreen_mode(mode: int) -> bool: return mode in FULLSCREEN_MODES  # invalid
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] `func` always needs a newline and an indented body.
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] If the real goal is fewer lines, though, the cleaner move is to drop the repeated `return false`
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] and collapse the guards into one return, using a cast so you don't need the `is` check to narrow
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] the type:
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:14 [deepseek-flash] func is_fullscreen_toggle_event(event: InputEvent) -> bool:
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 	var key_event := event as InputEventKey
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 	return key_event != null \
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 			and key_event.pressed \
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 			and not key_event.echo \
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 			and key_event.keycode == KEY_F12
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] The `and` short-circuits, so `key_event.pressed` is never touched when the cast fails. One return,
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] no inline calls, no repetition.
2026-09-13 09:33:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:52 [skid@archlinux] i would like to add line to source to inform my style a comment?
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.001 25.43KB 4.35s
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] Yes — a header comment is the usual way, since Godot ignores it and it costs nothing at runtime.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] Something like:
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] # Style: one call per statement — no inline call chains (e.g. get_viewport().foo()).
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] #        Prefer named helpers over inlining logic.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] #        Single-statement guards may sit on the `if` line; else-branches may not.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] #        Tabs for indentation.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] A few things to weigh:
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] - Keep it to the rules that aren't obvious. "Tabs" and "no inline calls" earn their place
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] because a reader can't infer them from the code below. "Use meaningful names" doesn't.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] - Header comments repeat. If every file carries the same block, edits mean touching every
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] file. A single `STYLE.md` (or `CONTRIBUTING.md`) at the repo root is the more standard home, and
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] each file can just point at it: `# Style: see STYLE.md`.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] - If the goal is enforcement, not documentation, a comment won't do it — `gdformat` /
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] `gdlint` (the gdtoolkit package) or an `.editorconfig` will actually hold the line and catch
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] violations. A comment only helps a human who reads it.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] Which are you after — a note for human readers, or something you want tooling to enforce? If it's
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] the former, tell me the exact rules you want stated and I'll tighten the wording.
2026-09-13 09:33:56 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:34:07 [skid@archlinux] tooooo verbose
2026-09-13 09:34:09 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.000 26.91KB 1.09s
2026-09-13 09:34:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:34:09 [deepseek-flash] # Style: no inline call chains; use named helpers.
2026-09-13 09:34:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:34:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:34:55 [skid@archlinux]  named helpers not inline call chains
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.000 27.21KB 1.83s
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] Good. That reads fine as-is — clear, one line, states the rule without the "Style:" prefix.
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] Only thing I'd check: it's terse enough that a reader may not know it means call chains
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] specifically (`get_viewport().set_input_as_handled()`), not e.g. `a.b` property access. If that
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] ambiguity ever bites, `# named helpers, not inline call chains` is the same length with a comma.
2026-09-13 09:34:57 [deepseek-flash] Otherwise leave it.
