2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] - This is a headless schema exporter. Run it with `--headless --script scrape.gd` and it dumps the
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] class list to JSON, then exits.
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] - It extends `SceneTree`, which is the standard way to write a command-line Godot tool that doesn't
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] need a main scene.
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Category overlap is present: every `Node` and `Resource` also inherits `Object`, so those classes
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] will appear in both the `node`/`resource` arrays and the `object` array. If you want mutually
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] exclusive categories, classify by the most specific ancestor first.
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Writing to `res://godot_api_schema.json` works from the project directory in editor/development
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] builds, but `res://` is read-only in exported projects. For a portable tool, accept an output path
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] argument or write to `user://` / the executable's base directory.
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `is_editor_class` includes `ResourceImporter`, which doesn't begin with `Editor` but is correctly
2026-09-13 11:53:33 [kimi-k2.7-code] grouped as editor-related.
