2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] In AWS web-based terminals (such as AWS CloudShell or EC2 Instance Connect), there is no desktop
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] "About" or application menu bar because the shell runs inside your web browser.
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] Depending on the terminal tool being used, colors can be adjusted through the following methods:
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. AWS CloudShell (Built-in Web Settings)
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] If using AWS CloudShell:
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Look at the top-right corner of the CloudShell pane (near the minimize/close buttons).
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Click the gear icon (Settings).
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • In the settings menu, there are options to adjust:
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Theme (Light vs. Dark)
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Font size
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. EC2 Instance Connect
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] EC2 Instance Connect's browser console does not provide a graphic settings menu for terminal
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] themes. To adjust colors there:
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Shell Prompt (`PS1`) and Highlights: Color changes must be made directly within your
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] shell configuration file (such as `~/.bashrc` or `~/.bash_profile`) using standard ANSI escape
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] codes.
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Directory Listing Colors: You can configure `LS_COLORS` or use `dircolors` to customize
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] file and folder color schemes.
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Browser Extension / Contrast: Browser-level high-contrast or dark-mode extensions will
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] also invert or restyle the canvas/terminal output.
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Alternative: Use a Local Terminal Client
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] For complete control over color schemes, palettes, and fonts:
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Connect to your EC2 instances or AWS environment using your local operating system's terminal
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] (e.g., iTerm2, Windows Terminal, Alacritty, GNOME Terminal) via SSH or the AWS Systems Manager
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] Session Manager plugin (`aws ssm start-session`).
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Local terminal emulators provide full GUI preferences for palettes, background colors, and
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] transparency.
2026-09-18 09:44:02 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
