2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] On Arch Linux, many terminal emulators (such as Alacritty, Kitty, Foot, rxvt-unicode, or the newer
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] GNOME Console) are intentionally minimalist and omit the traditional menu bar and "About" dialog
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] completely.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] To change color schemes on Arch, the method depends on which terminal application is running.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Identify Your Terminal Emulator
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can check which terminal process is currently active by checking your environment:
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • In your terminal, run: `echo TERM` or inspect the parent process with `ps -p PPID -o comm=`.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Common Arch Terminal Configuration Locations
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] Most minimalist terminals on Arch do not use a graphical settings dialog; their color palettes are
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] defined in plain-text configuration files under `~/.config/`:
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Alacritty
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Config file: `~/.config/alacritty/alacritty.toml` (or `.yml` on older versions).
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Colors are defined using hex values under the `[colors]` section, or by importing community
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] themes into the config file.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Kitty
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Config file: `~/.config/kitty/kitty.conf`.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Kitty includes an interactive theme picker: running `kitty +kitten themes` allows you to
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] preview and apply different color themes directly.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Foot (Wayland)
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Config file: `~/.config/foot/foot.ini`.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Foot includes preset theme files in `/usr/share/foot/themes/` which can be included in your
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] configuration.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • GNOME Console (`kgx`)
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Follows the system-wide GNOME color scheme (Light or Dark mode). You can also click the
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] hamburger menu (three horizontal lines) in the top-right corner to toggle between system, light,
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] and dark styles.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Xterm / URxvt
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Config file: `~/.Xresources` or `~/.Xdefaults`.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash]   * Colors are loaded using the `xrdb -merge ~/.Xresources` utility.
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you know the name of your specific terminal emulator, please share it, and precise instructions
2026-09-18 09:44:25 [gemini-3.8-flash] for updating its color palette can be provided.
