2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.004 4.604KB 4.43s
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] To identify which terminal emulator you are currently running from inside the shell, you can use
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] one of the following methods:
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Check the Parent Process
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] The most reliable method on Linux is to check the process that launched your current shell:
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] Run:
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] `ps -p (ps -o ppid= -p $) -o comm=`
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] This inspects the parent process of your current shell session and prints the executable name (for
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] example: `alacritty`, `kitty`, `foot`, or `gnome-terminal-server`).
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] Alternatively, if you have `psmisc` installed, you can view the full ancestry tree leading to your
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] current shell with:
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] `pstree -s $$`
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Check Environment Variables
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] Many modern terminals export their own identification variable into the environment. You can check
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] for these with:
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `echo $TERM_PROGRAM`
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `echo $TERMINAL`
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Note: Some minimalist emulators leave these unset, in which case checking the process hierarchy
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] with `ps` above is the best approach.)*
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Note: If you are currently inside a terminal multiplexer such as `tmux` or `screen`, the parent
2026-09-18 09:44:49 [gemini-3.8-flash] process will report `tmux` or `screen` rather than the graphical window.*
