2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.005 1.177KB 4.40s
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] To prepare `/dev/sda` for general storage on Arch Linux, the standard approach is to write a fresh
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] GPT partition table, create a partition spanning the full 2.7 TiB, and format it with a native
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Linux filesystem such as `ext4` or `btrfs`.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Before starting, ensure there is no data on `/dev/sda` that you need to retain, as this will erase
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] existing partition data.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Wipe and Partition the Disk
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can use `fdisk` to initialize a GPT partition table and create one large partition:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo fdisk /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Within the `fdisk` prompt:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Type `g` to create a new empty GPT partition table.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Type `n` to add a new partition (you can accept the default partition number, first sector, and
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] last sector to use the entire disk).
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Type `w` to write the table to disk and exit.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Alternatively, this can be done in a single non-interactive command using `parted`:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo parted /dev/sda --script mklabel gpt mkpart primary 0% 100%
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] This creates `/dev/sda1`.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Create the Filesystem
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Depending on your preference:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • For standard `ext4`:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   sudo mkfs.ext4 -L storage /dev/sda1
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] • For `btrfs` (supports snapshots and subvolumes):
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash]   sudo mkfs.btrfs -L storage /dev/sda1
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Mount and Set Ownership
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Create a mount point (for instance, `/mnt/storage`):
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo mkdir -p /mnt/storage
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo mount /dev/sda1 /mnt/storage
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] To give your user account (`skid`) write access to the mount root:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo chown -R skid:skid /mnt/storage
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 4. Automatic Mounting via `/etc/fstab` (Optional)
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] To mount the drive automatically on boot, retrieve its UUID:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] lsblk -f /dev/sda1
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Then append an entry to `/etc/fstab` using the UUID. For example, for an `ext4` system:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] UUID=<your-uuid-here>  /mnt/storage  ext4  defaults,noatime  0  2
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Or for `btrfs`:
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] UUID=<your-uuid-here>  /mnt/storage  btrfs  defaults,noatime,compress=zstd  0  0
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] Please let me know if you would like specific subvolume layouts (if using Btrfs), encryption via
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] LUKS, or help configuring `/etc/fstab`.
2026-09-18 10:50:23 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
