2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.005 3.616KB 4.73s
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] To verify the physical health of the drive and ensure all previous partition headers, metadata, or
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] encryption signatures (such as Windows BitLocker remnants) are completely cleared, you can perform
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] the following steps:
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. S.M.A.R.T. Health Check
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Install `smartmontools` if it is not already present:
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo pacman -S smartmontools
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Quick Assessment
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Check the overall health assessment and error log:
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo smartctl -H /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] To display the complete SMART attributes table (looking particularly at `Reallocated_Sector_Ct`,
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] `Current_Pending_Sector`, and `Offline_Uncorrectable`):
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo smartctl -A /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Self-Test
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can run an internal short or extended self-test:
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo smartctl -t short /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] Wait a few minutes, then view the results:
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo smartctl -l selftest /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (For an exhaustive physical scan, `sudo smartctl -t long /dev/sda` tests the entire platter
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] surface, which typically takes several hours on a 3 TB drive.)*
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:54 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Clearing Previous Signatures (BitLocker / Windows Metadata)
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] The `16M` partition (`sda1`) seen in your `lsblk` output is the standard Windows Microsoft Reserved
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] (MSR) partition, which strongly indicates the drive previously held a Windows volume (potentially
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] with BitLocker encryption on `sda2`).
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] To ensure every signature, superblock, and volume header is removed from the drive before creating
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] a new table:
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. View existing signatures:
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo wipefs /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Wipe all signatures across the drive and its partitions:
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo wipefs --all --force /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Surface Verification (Optional)
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you wish to test for bad blocks non-destructively across the entire surface before writing data:
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo badblocks -sv /dev/sda
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] Once verified and wiped clean with `wipefs`, the drive will be free of any previous headers or
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] encryption structures and ready for partitioning.
2026-09-18 10:52:55 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
