2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] Those directories in `/srv/http/grid` have a few distinct characteristics:
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Permissions (`drwx---rwx` / `707`)
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] Most of the directories (`aerialgrid`, `hd-aerialgrid`, `roagrid`, `topogrid`) have `drwx---rwx`
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] permissions:
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] • User (`http`): `rwx` (read, write, execute)
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Group (`http`): `---` (no permissions)
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Others (world): `rwx` (read, write, execute)
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] This is unusual because the group has zero access while any user on the system has full write
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] access. Usually, for a web server like Apache or Nginx running under the `http` user, you would
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] want directories set to `755` (`rwxr-xr-x`) like `sd-aerialgrid`, or group-shared permissions like
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] `775` (`rwxrwxr-x`) with your user added to the `http` group.
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Timestamps (`Jan 18 2026`)
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] The modification timestamps are set to future dates (January 2026). If you care about accurate file
2026-09-18 11:01:01 [gemini-3.8-flash] sorting by date or cache invalidation, you may want to touch them or verify your system clock.
