2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Fast, Clean Copy for Many Small Files
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] For millions or thousands of small files, `rsync` with the following flags is the safest and most
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] efficient tool. It preserves permissions, ownership, timestamps, and symlinks while avoiding
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] bottlenecks:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo rsync -aHAX --info=progress2 /srv/http/grid/ /mnt/grid26/
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Flag breakdown:*
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-a` (archive): Recursively copies and preserves permissions, timestamps, owners, groups, and
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] symlinks.
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-H`: Preserves hard links.
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-A`: Preserves ACLs (access control lists).
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `-X`: Preserves extended attributes.
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • `--info=progress2`: Gives a real-time aggregate transfer speed and overall percentage rather than
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] printing millions of individual filenames to the console (which slows down the transfer
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] significantly).
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 	Note on the trailing slashes:*
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 	sing `/srv/http/grid/` (with a trailing slash) places the subdirectories directly inside
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] `/mnt/grid26/` (e.g., `/mnt/grid26/aerialgrid`).
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. "Soft Mounting" (Bind Mount vs. Symlink)
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] In Linux, there are two standard ways to map `/srv/http/grid` to `/mnt/grid26`:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option A: Bind Mount (Recommended for Web Servers)
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] A bind mount makes `/mnt/grid26` appear directly at `/srv/http/grid` at the filesystem level. Web
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] servers (Nginx, Apache, Caddy) handle bind mounts transparently without needing special settings
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] for symlink following or security restrictions.
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Once the transfer completes and you are satisfied:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    # Move old data out of the way or back it up
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo mv /srv/http/grid /srv/http/grid.bak
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo mkdir -p /srv/http/grid
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Test the bind mount:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo mount --bind /mnt/grid26 /srv/http/grid
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Make it permanent in `/etc/fstab` (append to the end of the file):
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    /mnt/grid26    /srv/http/grid    none    bind    0    0
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option B: Symlink (Soft Link)
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you prefer a traditional symbolic link:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Move or remove the original folder:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo mv /srv/http/grid /srv/http/grid.bak
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Create the link:
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash]    sudo ln -s /mnt/grid26 /srv/http/grid
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Note: If using a symlink, ensure your web server configuration allows following symlinks, e.g.,
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] `Options FollowSymLinks` in Apache or proper root handling in Nginx).*
2026-09-18 11:03:52 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
