2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] Yes, `pv` stands for Pipe Viewer. It is a small terminal utility that monitors the flow of
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] data through a pipe (`|`).
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] It shows:
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • A progress bar and percentage (if size is known)
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Transfer speed (e.g., `45.2MB/s`)
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Total data transferred so far
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] • An ETA timer
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] It is not installed by default, but it is available in the official Arch repositories:
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] sudo pacman -S pv
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] Running without `pv`
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you don't want to install extra tools, you do not need it. The standard `tar` command works
2026-09-18 11:06:24 [gemini-3.8-flash] completely fine on its own:
