2026-09-18 11:07:35 [skid@archlinux] is sync sudo or no?
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪣 0.7° $0.005 23.34KB 1.68s
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] No, `sync` does not require `sudo`.
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] Any standard user can run `sync`. When invoked, it requests that the Linux kernel flush all dirty
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] file system buffers across the entire system out to physical storage.
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] You can simply run:
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] sync
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] When the command exits and returns your shell prompt, all pending writes are safely committed to
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] the disk.
2026-09-18 11:07:37 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
