2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] Option 1: Using the `progress` utility
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] There is a dedicated utility named `progress` (formerly known as `cv` / Coreutils Viewer).
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] It searches `/proc` for running coreutils/tar commands and shows their current file position and
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] throughput.
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you install it via `sudo pacman -S progress`, you can simply run:
2026-09-18 11:09:07 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
