2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] Thanks for sharing these. The project appears to be a native Linux embedded host/service layer for
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] a DSP/remote-control stack (`dsptool`), mixing system interfaces, networking, media I/O, and an
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] HTTP RPC front end.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] A few high-level observations:
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] • Architecture*
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - The codebase is mostly header-only and compiled into a small number of `.cpp` entry points
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] (`fit3.cpp`, `displaytest.cpp`, `nativetool.cpp`, `opensocket.cpp`). That keeps builds simple but
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] gives each translation unit a very large include surface.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - A central `Stereo` singleton in `headless.h` owns Redis/Valkey, process management, and event
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] routing, while `fit3.cpp` sets up the HTTP and signal handling. Several subsystems still carry
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] older names (`Stereo`, `nitrohost`, `bios`) alongside newer ones (`fit3`).
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] • Notable subsystem notes*
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `alsaaudio.h` — wraps card enumeration and simple PCM playback/capture tests. There is a
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] hard-coded test that opens `"default"` and writes generated square-wave audio.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `drmdisplay.h` / `eglgraphics.h` — KMS/GBM/EGL init path for headless GLES output. Some teardown
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] paths are commented out and the flip path still does a full `drmModeSetCrtc` each frame rather than
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] true atomic/page-flip double buffering.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `headless.h` — contains a `Process` class that forks child apps and pipes stdio. It also hosts
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] the JSON-RPC dispatcher (`InvokeRPC`). The dispatcher is a long `if/else` chain that could be
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] table-driven if it keeps growing.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `http.h` — small threaded HTTP server with POST-based RPC and static file serving. It has
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] path-sanitization checks (`..`) and a keep-alive path, and it sets a 3-second receive timeout per
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] connection.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `redis.h` — synchronous hiredis wrapper plus async `Scribe`/`Sink` helpers. The async paths start
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] threads that are never joined.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `json.h` — custom JSON parser. It distinguishes `Integer` from `Number` and uses `wchar_t` /
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] `codecvt_utf8` internally.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `crypto.h` — provides SHA-512 via OpenSSL EVP (and labels it `sha3_512` in the EVP path) or
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] Common Crypto on macOS.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] • Things worth tightening if you plan to extend this*
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Many places use raw `new` and never `delete` (e.g., `Process`, `HttpConnection`, `JSValue`
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] subtrees in the RPC dispatcher). For a long-running daemon that matters.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Several functions ignore return values or partially handle errors (common in bring-up code, but
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] easy to harden).
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - Globals/statics such as `fd`, `buffers`, `frame_data` in `video.h` make that module
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] non-reentrant.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `headless.h` line `utf8 src="stereo.h " Stringify(__line__);` is almost certainly not what was
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] intended; `Stringify(__line__)` expands to `"__line__"`, not the current line number. Use
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] `std::to_string(__LINE__)` instead.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `crypto.h` EVP path calls `EVP_sha3_512()` while the function name says SHA-512. If you want
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] SHA-512, use `EVP_sha512()`; if you want SHA3-512, rename the function to avoid confusion.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] - `base64.h` decode routine does not validate padding or reject non-alphabet characters, and the
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] encode/decode alphabets differ (`+` vs `,`), which is intentional per the comment but easy to trip
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] over.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] If you want, I can look deeper at any specific area — for example, converting the RPC dispatcher to
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] a registration table, hardening the Redis lifecycle, or finishing the DRM atomic/page-flip path.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] Just let me know which files or problems are current.
2026-09-18 19:05:30 [kimi-k2.7-code] 
