2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] On Arch Linux, the removal command depends on which "Sticky Notes" package you actually have
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] installed. Here's how to find and remove it:
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Find the package name
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] pacman -Qs sticky
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] or search more broadly:
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] pacman -Qs notes
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] If you installed it from the AUR (common ones: `sticky-notes`, `xpad`, `indicator-stickynotes`),
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] use `yay`/`paru` instead of `pacman` for querying — they share the same query flags.
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. Common candidates and their removal commands
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] • If it's the Flatpak "Sticky Notes" (com.vixalien.sticky-notes) or similar GNOME extension
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] app:*
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] flatpak uninstall com.vixalien.sticky-notes
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] • If it's `xpad` (classic X11 sticky notes):*
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] sudo pacman -Rns xpad
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] • If it's a GNOME Shell extension (e.g. "Sticky Notes" from extensions.gnome.org):*
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] gnome-extensions uninstall sticky-notes@blob.blob.gmail.com
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] (the exact UUID varies — check `gnome-extensions list`)
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] • If it's an AUR package:*
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] yay -Rns sticky-notes
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] # or
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] paru -Rns sticky-notes
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. General uninstall pattern for pacman
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] Once you know the exact package name, `-Rns` removes the package, its dependencies not needed
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] elsewhere, and its config/cache files:
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] sudo pacman -Rns <package-name>
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] If you tell me exactly how you installed it (pacman, AUR helper, Flatpak, Snap, GNOME extension, or
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] a manually built app), I can give you the precise command.
2026-09-18 19:24:55 [claude-sonnet-5] 
