2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] with a hardcoded binary path per current code, but confirm no code path allows the `name`/`guid`
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] parameters to influence the executable or arguments launched. `sys.write` forwards arbitrary bytes
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] to a connected process's stdin — test for terminal escape sequence injection (the JS client already
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] strips some ANSI codes defensively; verify server-side output isn't independently exploitable) and
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] for using this channel to pivot into shell command execution on any spawned interactive shell.
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] - `sys.setclock` — accepts attacker-controlled epoch millis and calls `settimeofday`. Test
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] authorization boundary (should require root — confirm process privilege level) and downstream
2026-09-18 19:47:39 [claude-sonnet-5] effects on TLS cert validation, log timestamps, and session-expiry logic elsewhere in the stack.
