2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] If you want BunnyCDN to send `Accept-Encoding: gzip` on its origin pull requests, that's configured
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] in the Pull Zone settings, but there's a simpler and more reliable fix that doesn't depend on
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] CDN-side header behavior at all — worth considering first.
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] • Recommended: fix it on the origin (nginx) side with `gunzip on;`*
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] This makes nginx serve the `.gz` file regardless of what `Accept-Encoding` header the requester
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] sends (whether that's BunnyCDN, a browser, or anything else):
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] location /roagrid/ {
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 	add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin *;
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 	add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable";
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 	root /mnt/grid26;
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 	gzip_static on;
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 	gunzip on;
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] Check the module is available first:
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] nginx -V 2>&1 | grep -o http_gunzip_module
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] This way you don't need to rely on BunnyCDN's origin request headers being correct — it'll work no
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] matter what.
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] • If you still want to configure BunnyCDN's side:*
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] In the Bunny dashboard, under your Pull Zone settings, look in:
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] - Caching tab — there may be an option related to forwarding headers or compression
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] handling.
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] - Origin settings — sometimes labeled something like "Forward Accept-Encoding" or "Origin
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] compression".
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] I'm not fully confident on the exact current label/location since Bunny's dashboard UI changes
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] fairly often — I'd suggest searching their docs for `Accept-Encoding` or `gzip` specifically to get
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] the precise current setting name, rather than me guessing and sending you to the wrong tab.
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] • My suggestion:* apply `gunzip on;` on your nginx config now (quick, guaranteed fix), and
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] treat the BunnyCDN setting as optional/secondary — it removes a dependency on CDN behavior that
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] might change or vary per request type.
2026-09-18 21:31:23 [claude-sonnet-5] 
