2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] Yes — logging the PID at startup makes it much easier to correlate with `/proc/<pid>/limits` and
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] `/proc/<pid>/fd` when debugging the fd exhaustion you hit earlier, without needing `pidof` and
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] hoping there's only one instance running.
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] • Minimal version (C/C++):*
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <unistd.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <stdio.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] static void logStartupPid() {
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	pid_t pid = getpid();
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	printf("pid:%d\n", pid);
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] Call `logStartupPid()` early in `main()`, right after your version/copyright banner.
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] • Slightly more useful version — also writes a pidfile*, so external tooling (or a quick
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] shell check) doesn't need to grep logs:
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <unistd.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <stdio.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <string.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] #include <errno.h>
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] static void writePidFile(const char *path) {
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	FILE *f = fopen(path, "w");
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	if (!f) {
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 		fprintf(stderr, "writePidFile failed for %s errno:%d:%s\n",
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 			path, errno, strerror(errno));
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 		return;
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	}
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	fprintf(f, "%d\n", getpid());
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	fclose(f);
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] static void logStartupPid(const char *pidFilePath) {
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	pid_t pid = getpid();
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	printf("pid:%d\n", pid);
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	if (pidFilePath) {
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 		writePidFile(pidFilePath);
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 	}
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] Then at startup:
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
