2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] Since your log already opens `Stereo.logFD = 3`, you clearly have fd tracing in place — printing
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] the PID alongside that gives you a complete picture (which process, how many fds, what limit) with
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] no extra tooling. If you're launching this via `host.sh` and eventually via systemd, consider also
2026-09-18 22:25:30 [claude-sonnet-5] having `logStartupPid` write to a path that matches a `PIDFile=` directive in the unit, so systemd
