2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] Preventing Chrome's Right-Click Context Menu on Canvas
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] To disable the default right-click context menu on a canvas element, listen for the `contextmenu`
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] event and prevent its default behavior.
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] Basic Solution
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] function disableCanvasContextMenu(canvasElement) {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	canvasElement.addEventListener("contextmenu", handleContextMenu);
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] function handleContextMenu(event) {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	event.preventDefault();
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] Usage:
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] const canvas = document.getElementById("myCanvas");
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] disableCanvasContextMenu(canvas);
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] HTML Alternative
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] You can also do this directly in HTML:
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] <canvas id="myCanvas" oncontextmenu="return false;"></canvas>
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] If You Still Want a Custom Menu
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] If you want to replace the browser menu with your own custom actions, you can build one manually:
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] function setupCustomContextMenu(canvasElement, menuElement) {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	canvasElement.addEventListener("contextmenu", (event) => {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 		event.preventDefault();
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 		showCustomMenu(menuElement, event.clientX, event.clientY);
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	});
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	document.addEventListener("click", () => {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 		hideCustomMenu(menuElement);
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	});
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] function showCustomMenu(menuElement, x, y) {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	menuElement.style.left = `${x}px`;
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	menuElement.style.top = `${y}px`;
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	menuElement.style.display = "block";
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] function hideCustomMenu(menuElement) {
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 	menuElement.style.display = "none";
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] A Note on Limitations
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] This only prevents the right-click context menu. It won't stop:
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] - Users from taking a screenshot
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] - Browser DevTools access to canvas pixel data (via `getImageData` or `toDataURL`)
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] - Keyboard shortcuts like saving via browser menus
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] If your goal is to protect image content from being saved/extracted, `contextmenu` prevention is
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] only a minor deterrent — there's no fully reliable way to stop a determined user from capturing
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] canvas content in a browser.
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] Let me know if you're trying to solve a specific use case (like protecting artwork or building a
2026-09-19 13:21:08 [claude-sonnet-5] drawing app), and I can suggest a more tailored approach.
