2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Understanding the "Tainted Canvas" WebGL Error
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] (Side note: your message had a stray `[200~` at the start — that's a leftover bracketed-paste
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] terminal artifact, not an actual error code. No need to worry about it.)
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] What This Error Means
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Uncaught SecurityError: Failed to execute 'texImage2D' on 'WebGL2RenderingContext':
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Tainted canvases may not be loaded.
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] This happens when you try to load an image, video, or another canvas into a WebGL texture,
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] but the browser has marked that source as "tainted" due to cross-origin restrictions.
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] A canvas/image becomes "tainted" when it contains pixel data loaded from a different origin
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] without proper CORS permission. Once tainted, the browser blocks WebGL from reading its
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] pixel data — this is a security measure to prevent silently stealing image data from other sites.
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Common Causes
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Loading an image from a CDN (like BunnyCDN) that doesn't send CORS headers
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. Missing `crossOrigin` attribute on the `<img>` element
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. Drawing a cross-origin image onto a 2D `<canvas>` first, then trying to use that canvas as a
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] WebGL texture
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 4. Loading local files via `file://` protocol
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] How to Fix It
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Set `crossOrigin` on the Image Before Loading
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] function loadImageForTexture(url, onLoad) {
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const image = new Image();
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 	image.crossOrigin = "anonymous";
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 	image.onload = () => onLoad(image);
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 	image.src = url;
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] • Important: `crossOrigin` must be set before* `src` is assigned.
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. Ensure the Server Sends CORS Headers
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] The image server (BunnyCDN in your case) needs to respond with:
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] • On BunnyCDN*, you can enable this in your Pull Zone settings:
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] - Go to your Pull Zone → Headers
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] - Add a custom header:
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Or restrict it to your specific domain instead of `*` if you want tighter security:
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://yourdomain.com
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. Double-Check Both Sides Match
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] CORS requires both:
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] - ✅ `crossOrigin` set on the client-side `Image` object
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] - ✅ `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header from the server
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] If either is missing, the canvas becomes tainted.
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] Quick Debugging Checklist
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] ╭─────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────╮
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Check                                  │  Status    │
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] ├─────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────┤
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] │  image.crossOrigin = "anonymous" set?   │  ?         │
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Server sends Access-Control-Allow-*?   │  ?         │
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Are you loading from BunnyCDN domain?  │  ?         │
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Same headers present on redirect URLs? │  ?         │
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] ╰─────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────╯
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-19 13:48:11 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
