2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] `ls` Sorted by Creation Date, One Name Per Line
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ls -1t
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - `-t` sorts by modification time (newest first)
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - `-1` keeps it to one filename per line
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Oldest First (Reverse Order)
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ls -1tr
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] A Note on "Creation Date" vs "Modification Date"
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] On most Linux systems, `ls -t` sorts by modification time, not true creation time — Linux
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] filesystems (like ext4) often don't track a separate "birth time" the way macOS does.
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] • On macOS*, you can get true creation time with:
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ls -1tU
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] • On Linux*, if your filesystem supports it (e.g., ext4 with `statx`), you can check true
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] birth time with `stat`:
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] stat --format="%W %n" *
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Or sort by birth time using `find`:
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] find . -maxdepth 1 -type f -printf "%C@ %f\n" | sort -n | cut -d' ' -f2-
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Quick Reference
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ╭──────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-20 09:03:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Command     │  Behavior                            │
