2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] KDE Menu Editor "Delete" — What It Actually Does
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] • Short answer: No, it won't uninstall the package.*
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] What Menu Editor's Delete Actually Does
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] KDE's Menu Editor (`kmenuedit`) only manages `.desktop` files — the shortcuts/entries that
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] make apps appear in your application launcher. Clicking Delete there:
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] - ✅ Removes the app's icon/entry from your Kickoff/Application menu
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] - ❌ Does NOT remove the actual Falkon binary
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] - ❌ Does NOT free up disk space
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] - ❌ Does NOT remove dependencies
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] The program will still be fully installed and runnable from a terminal (`falkon`) or via `krunner`
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] (Alt+Space) even after deleting it from the menu.
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] Why This Distinction Matters
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] ╭─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────┬──────────────────────╮
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Action                     │  Removes from Menu   │  Uninstalls Package  │
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] ├─────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] │  `kmenuedit` → Delete       │  ✅ Yes               │  ❌ No                │
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] │  `sudo pacman -Rns falkon`  │  ✅ Yes (indirectly)  │  ✅ Yes               │
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] ╰─────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────┴──────────────────────╯
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] Pacman removal will also clean up the menu entry automatically, since the `.desktop` file
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] is part of the package.
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] Recommendation
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] If your goal is to actually uninstall Falkon (not just hide it), stick with:
2026-09-20 09:35:36 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] sudo pacman -Rns falkon
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] Only use Menu Editor's Delete if you want to keep the program installed but just hide it from the
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] app launcher (e.g., you use it occasionally via terminal but don't want menu clutter).
2026-09-20 09:35:37 [claude-sonnet-5] 
