2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Recap: Should Home Users Bother Uninstalling Falkon?
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Good question. Here's the honest breakdown:
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Most Home Users: Probably Not Worth It
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Falkon is a lightweight browser (QtWebEngine-based) — it's small, uses minimal disk space,
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] and doesn't run any background services when you're not using it. For most people, leaving it
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] installed but unused causes zero practical harm:
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - No background processes eating RAM
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - No noticeable disk space impact (a few MB)
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - Won't slow down boot time or menu loading
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] When It Does Make Sense to Remove
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ╭─────────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────╮
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Situation                              │  Worth Removing?    │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ├─────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Just want a cleaner app menu           │  Use kmenuedit hide │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Minimal/embedded system, low storage   │  Yes                │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Security concern (unused browser)      │  Yes                │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  "I'll never use it, why is it here"    │  Optional/cosmetic  │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] │  It's part of kde-network-meta bundle   │  Usually leave it   │
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ╰─────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────╯
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Better Option for Most People: Just Hide It
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] If your actual goal is just "I don't want to see it in my menu" rather than reclaiming disk
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] space, the simpler and safer path is:
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] kmenuedit → select Falkon → Delete
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] This keeps the package installed (so no dependency conflicts with `kde-network-meta`), but removes
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] the icon clutter from your launcher — which is probably the actual annoyance, not disk usage.
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Bottom Line
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Unless you're short on storage or have a specific reason (security policy, minimal install, etc.),
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] it's not really necessary to fight the dependency chain just to remove an unused ~10MB
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] browser. Hiding it from the menu solves the everyday annoyance with zero risk.
2026-09-20 09:39:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
