2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Splash Screens — Two Different Things
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Plasma Login/Startup Splash Screen
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] This is the animated logo that appears briefly when you log into Plasma (before your desktop
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] loads).
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] • To change it:*
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - Open System Settings → Startup and Shutdown → Splash Screen
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - Choose a theme from the list (KDE ships several, like "None," "Breeze," etc.)
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] - You can also download more via the "Get New Splash Screens" button (uses KDE Store)
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Or via terminal, check available ones:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] plasma-apply-splashscreen --list
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Apply one:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] plasma-apply-splashscreen org.kde.breeze.desktop
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. Boot Splash Screen (Plymouth)
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] This is the graphical screen shown during boot, before Plasma even starts — replacing the
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] wall of text output.
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Arch doesn't include this by default; you have to install and configure Plymouth:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] sudo pacman -S plymouth
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Then:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Add `plymouth` to your `mkinitcpio.conf` hooks (before `filesystems`):
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5]    HOOKS=(base udev plymouth autodetect modconf block filesystems keyboard fsck)
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. Regenerate initramfs:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5]    sudo mkinitcpio -P
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. Add kernel parameter `splash` to your bootloader config (e.g., GRUB or systemd-boot)
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 4. Choose/install a Plymouth theme:
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5]    plymouth-set-default-theme -l
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5]    sudo plymouth-set-default-theme -R bgrt
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] Which one are you actually after — the login splash (Plasma) or the boot splash
2026-09-20 09:51:32 [claude-sonnet-5] (Plymouth, the one during startup before login)?
