2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.025 11.49KB 19.21s
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] Tainted canvas errors happen when an image is drawn onto a `<canvas>` without proper CORS clearance
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] — even if your origin server sends the right headers, there are several places this can break down,
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] especially with a CDN in front.
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Client-Side: Set `crossOrigin` on the Image
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] This is the most commonly missed step. Even if the server sends `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`,
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] the browser won't apply it unless you explicitly request it:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] function loadImage(url) {
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 		const img = new Image();
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 		img.crossOrigin = "anonymous"; // Must be set BEFORE img.src
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 		img.onload = () => resolve(img);
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 		img.onerror = reject;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 		img.src = url;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	});
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] If `crossOrigin` isn't set, the browser treats the image as opaque for canvas purposes regardless
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] of server headers.
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. CDN Header Stripping/Caching Issue
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] This is very likely your actual problem. Here's why:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] - Many CDNs cache the response the first time it's fetched
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] - If that first request didn't include an `Origin` header (or came from a different context), the
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] cached response might not have `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` attached — and the CDN may serve
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] that cached version to everyone afterward, headers included
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] - Some CDNs also strip custom headers by default unless explicitly configured to pass them through
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] • Fix:* Add `Vary: Origin` so caches don't serve a CORS-less response to a CORS request:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] location /aerialgrid/ {
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	add_header Access-Control-Allow-Origin *;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	add_header Vary Origin;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	add_header Cache-Control "public, max-age=31536000, immutable";
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	tcp_nopush on;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	sendfile on;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	sendfile_max_chunk 4m;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	root /mnt/grid26;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] Then purge the CDN cache for `/aerialgrid/*` and test again — if the CDN cached a bad
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] response before your `add_header` was in place, no client-side fix will help until that cache
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] clears.
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. Verify Headers Are Actually Reaching the Browser
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] Don't trust — verify. Check what's actually being returned through the CDN, not directly
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] from your origin:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] curl -I https://your-cdn-domain.com/aerialgrid/example.png
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] Look specifically for:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] access-control-allow-origin: *
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] If it's missing when going through the CDN (but present when hitting your origin directly), the CDN
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] is stripping it — this is common with CDNs that don't pass through unrecognized/custom headers by
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] default.
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 4. Double-Check the Draw Sequence
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] Make sure you're not accidentally reading pixel data before the image fully loads, or mixing
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] tainted and untainted sources on the same canvas:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] async function drawFromCDN(canvas, url) {
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const img = await loadImage(url); // uses crossOrigin version above
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	ctx.drawImage(img, 0, 0);
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	// This will now succeed if CORS was properly honored:
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const pixelData = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 	return pixelData;
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] If any single image drawn to that canvas was loaded without proper CORS clearance, the
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] entire canvas becomes tainted — even for later, well-behaved draws.
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-20 09:57:24 [claude-sonnet-5] 
