2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.029 15.22KB 19.38s
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Good question to raise — yes, there are a few things worth being aware of if you're moving
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] pixel-drawing work into Web Workers, especially since you're already dealing with CORS/tainting.
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 1. Workers Don't Have `Image()` or Direct DOM Access
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Inside a worker, you can't use `new Image()` — there's no DOM. Instead, you use `fetch()` +
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] `createImageBitmap()`:
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] async function loadImageBitmap(url) {
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const response = await fetch(url, { mode: "cors" });
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const blob = await response.blob();
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	return createImageBitmap(blob);
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 2. CORS Rules Still Apply — Same Tainting Logic
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Even in a worker, if the fetch doesn't have proper CORS headers, the resulting `ImageBitmap` can
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] still be tainted when drawn to an `OffscreenCanvas`. The `mode: "cors"` option on `fetch()`
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] is the worker-equivalent of setting `img.crossOrigin = "anonymous"` on the main thread.
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] function drawInWorker(bitmap, canvas) {
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	ctx.drawImage(bitmap, 0, 0);
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	// Still throws if tainted, same as main thread:
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const pixels = ctx.getImageData(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	return pixels;
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] }
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 3. `OffscreenCanvas` Support
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] If you're rendering inside the worker itself (rather than just processing data), you'll want
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] `OffscreenCanvas`, transferred from the main thread:
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] // Main thread
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] const canvas = document.querySelector("canvas");
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] const offscreen = canvas.transferControlToOffscreen();
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] worker.postMessage({ canvas: offscreen }, [offscreen]);
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] // worker.js
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] self.onmessage = (e) => {
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const canvas = e.data.canvas;
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	const ctx = canvas.getContext("2d");
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 	// draw as normal
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] };
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Support is solid in modern Chromium and Firefox; Safari lagged behind for a while but has caught up
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] in recent versions — worth checking your minimum target browser if "cross-platform" includes older
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Safari/WebKit-based environments (e.g., embedded webviews).
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 4. Transferring Data Back to Main Thread
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] Pixel data (`ImageData`, `ArrayBuffer`, `ImageBitmap`) should be sent using transferable
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] objects, not structured-cloned copies — this avoids expensive memory duplication:
2026-09-20 10:15:01 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] // Worker side
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] self.postMessage({ imageData }, [imageData.data.buffer]);
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 5. If You Ever Want `SharedArrayBuffer` (High-Performance Pixel Sharing)
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] This requires your server to send cross-origin isolation headers:
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] This is a stricter requirement than plain CORS and would also apply to your CDN-served images —
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] likely unnecessary unless you're doing heavy real-time pixel manipulation across threads.
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] • Bottom line: Web Workers don't introduce new tainting rules — they enforce
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] the same* CORS rules you already fixed, just via `fetch(mode: "cors")` instead of
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] `img.crossOrigin`. The main things to watch are (a) using `createImageBitmap` instead of `Image`,
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] and (b) transferable objects for performance.
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] Are you planning to do the actual `drawImage`/pixel manipulation inside the worker (via
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] `OffscreenCanvas`), or just fetch/decode there and send bitmaps back to the main thread for
2026-09-20 10:15:02 [claude-sonnet-5] drawing?
