2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.3 claude-sonnet-5 A\ 🪠 🧊 $0.363 514.7KB 17.91s
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] Yes — `crossOrigin` is a standard DOM property, defined in the HTML Living Standard
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] (WHATWG), not something browser-specific or informal.
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] Where It's Specified
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] It's part of the CORS settings attributes spec, which the WHATWG HTML spec defines here:
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 	ttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/urls-and-fetching.html#cors-settings-attributes
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] It applies to several elements beyond just `<img>`:
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] - `<img crossorigin>`
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] - `<script crossorigin>`
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] - `<link crossorigin>`
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] - `<video>` / `<audio>`
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] - `<use>` (SVG)
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] Valid Values (Per Spec)
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] ╭───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] │  Value                │  Meaning                                                                 │
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] ├───────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] │  `"anonymous"`        │  Send CORS request **without credentials** (no cookies)                  │
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] │  `"use-credentials"`  │  Send CORS request **with credentials** (cookies, HTTP auth)             │
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] │  *(missing/omitted)*  │  No CORS mode — regular request, canvas becomes tainted if cross-origin  │
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] ╰───────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] The "Invalid Value Default" Rule
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] This is the part that explains why `"dsptool"` in your code worked anyway. The spec defines
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] `crossOrigin` as an enumerated attribute with this exact rule:
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 	he invalid value default and missing value default are both the Anonymous
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] state.
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] So per spec: any string that isn't `"use-credentials"` — including typos, garbage strings,
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] or `"dsptool"` — is treated identically to `"anonymous"`. This isn't a browser quirk or fallback
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] hack; it's literally specified behavior, consistent across Chrome/Firefox/Safari.
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] Practical Takeaway
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] image.crossOrigin = "anonymous";     // ✅ explicit, correct
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] image.crossOrigin = "dsptool";       // ✅ works, but only by spec coincidence
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] image.crossOrigin = "use-credentials"; // ⚠️ different mode, requires server ACAO to not be "*"
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] image.crossOrigin = null;            // same as not setting it — no CORS mode at all
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] So your existing code isn't relying on undefined behavior — it's technically spec-compliant, just
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] misleading to read. Worth fixing for clarity, but not for correctness.
2026-09-20 11:12:33 [claude-sonnet-5] 
