2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] That is acceptable for local development, but `.gitignore` only prevents accidental Git tracking—it
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] does not encrypt or hide the key.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] Recommended precautions:
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Ensure `./apikey` is actually ignored with `git check-ignore ./apikey`.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Restrict permissions: `chmod 600 ./apikey`.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Grant Deno only the necessary permission: `--allow-read=./apikey`, plus restricted `--allow-net`
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] for the Bunny endpoint.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Read it server-side only and trim the trailing newline.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Do not include it in container images, deployments, logs, errors, or responses.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Prefer an environment variable or hosting secret manager for production.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Remember that `./apikey` is relative to the process’s current working directory, not necessarily
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] the source file.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] - If it was ever committed—even briefly—remove it from Git history and rotate the Bunny key. Adding
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] it to `.gitignore` afterward is insufficient.
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] Also avoid serving the project directory itself as a static web root, since a server
2026-09-22 08:49:17 [gpt-5.6-sol] misconfiguration could expose the file.
