2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] It depends what you mean by “connect” to the Bunny pull zone:
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Fetch content from a public pull-zone URL: no API key is needed.
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Manage or purge the pull zone through Bunny’s API: use your Bunny account API key
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] in the `AccessKey` HTTP header. Keep this server-side in Deno.
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Access a pull zone with Token Authentication enabled: use the pull zone’s Token
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] Authentication Key to generate a short-lived signed URL server-side. Never send that key to
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] browsers.
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Upload files to the origin Storage Zone: use the Storage Zone password/API key,
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] not the pull-zone key, with the Bunny Storage API.
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] Your `./apikey` file can hold the appropriate secret during local development. The main account API
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] key is powerful, so use the token-auth or storage-specific key when that is all you need.
2026-09-22 08:50:13 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:55 [skid@archlinux] what is term for un caching refreshing a file i have changed on server
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.024 17.53KB 3.56s
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] The usual term is cache invalidation.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] For Bunny.net specifically:
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Purge cache — remove a cached file so Bunny fetches the changed version from the origin.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Purge URL — invalidate one particular file.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Purge zone cache — invalidate everything in the pull zone.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Cache busting — change the URL, often with a version or query parameter, such as
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] `image.jpg?v=2`, to bypass the old cached entry.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] For a file changed at the same URL, you generally want to purge that URL from the Bunny CDN
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] cache.
2026-09-22 08:50:59 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
