2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] • Code - OSS is the open-source base of Visual Studio Code*.
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] Microsoft association
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] - The source project is primarily developed by Microsoft and community contributors.
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] - It is published at [`microsoft/vscode`](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode) under the MIT
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] licence.
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Microsoft builds that source into the branded Visual Studio Code product, adding
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] Microsoft branding, distribution terms, telemetry configuration, and access to Microsoft’s
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] extension marketplace.
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Arch Linux’s `code` package is generally an independently compiled Code - OSS build
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] rather than Microsoft’s official binary.
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:56:37 [gpt-5.6-sol] Your version information therefore looks like an Arch-packaged build of the VS Code source.
