2026-09-22 08:57:40 [skid@archlinux] if i wish to brand similar to way microsoft do it, should i look at what level, arch distro? or below that?
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.047 22.17KB 15.96s
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] Brand it at the application/source-build level, below the Arch distribution packaging
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] layer.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] A sensible structure is:
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 1. Fork `microsoft/vscode`
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Keep your product-specific changes and update strategy there.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- The source is MIT-licensed, but Microsoft names, logos, and other trademarks are separate.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 2. Configure the product identity
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Edit the build’s `product.json` values: product name, application name, data-directory name, URL
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] protocol, server names, and related identifiers.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Replace icons, splash/branding assets, desktop-entry details, and About-page information.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Use unique application and data-directory names so it can coexist with Code - OSS and VS Code.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 3. Choose your services
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Configure your own update mechanism, telemetry policy, documentation URLs, issue tracker, and
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] crash-reporting services.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Do not assume that a custom distribution may use Microsoft’s Visual Studio Marketplace. Many
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] community builds use Open VSX, subject to its own terms.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Copilot and other Microsoft/GitHub services have their own licensing and distribution
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] conditions.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 4. Package it for Arch
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Use a `PKGBUILD` to build/install your branded application.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- The Arch package should mainly handle dependencies, installation paths, desktop entries, icons,
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] MIME handlers, and package metadata.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	- Avoid making the Arch packaging scripts the sole location for substantial product changes unless
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] it is only a small personal build.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] So the layers are roughly:
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] • Code - OSS source → your branded build → Arch package*
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] For a quick personal experiment, applying patches from a custom `PKGBUILD` is reasonable. For a
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] product you intend to maintain or distribute, keep the branding in a source fork/build
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] configuration and let the Arch package merely package the resulting product.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] Also choose names and artwork that cannot be mistaken for Visual Studio Code, and retain
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] the MIT licence and applicable third-party notices when distributing it.
2026-09-22 08:57:57 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:21 [skid@archlinux] if i wish to target my developer tools at windows and macos also?
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.045 24.43KB 11.04s
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Then keep the branding and functionality at the Code - OSS source/product level, and treat
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Arch, Windows, and macOS as separate packaging targets:
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] • Code - OSS fork → shared branded product → platform-specific builds/installers*
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Shared application layer
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Maintain these once in your fork/build configuration:
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - `product.json` identity and application names
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Branding, icons and About information
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Extensions bundled with your product
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Developer-tool features
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Telemetry and privacy settings
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Update-service configuration
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Extension registry, such as Open VSX
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Unique URL protocol and user-data directories
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Avoid putting core branding only in an Arch `PKGBUILD`, because it would then need to be recreated
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] for every operating system.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Platform-specific distribution
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] • Windows*
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Build x64 and, if needed, ARM64 versions.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Produce an `.exe` or MSI installer.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Use unique application IDs and installation directories.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Sign executables and installers with an Authenticode code-signing certificate.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Account for Windows Defender/SmartScreen reputation.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] • macOS*
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Build separate Apple Silicon and Intel versions, or a universal application.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Use your own reverse-domain bundle identifier.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Sign with an Apple Developer ID certificate.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Enable the appropriate hardened-runtime settings.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Notarize and staple the application.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Distribute as a signed `.dmg`, `.pkg`, or archive.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] • Linux*
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Provide packages such as Arch `PKGBUILD`, `.deb`, `.rpm`, AppImage or Flatpak.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Configure desktop entries, icons, MIME associations and protocol handlers.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Build infrastructure
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Use CI workers native to each target:
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Linux runner for Linux
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Windows runner for Windows
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - macOS runner for macOS
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Keep signing certificates and notarization credentials in protected CI secrets. Builds from
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] untrusted pull requests should never receive those secrets.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] Important service and licensing points
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] The Code - OSS source is MIT-licensed, but Microsoft’s trademarks, artwork, marketplace access,
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] update infrastructure and proprietary extensions are separate. In particular:
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Use your own product name and visual identity.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Do not assume access to Microsoft’s Visual Studio Marketplace.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Consider Open VSX or your own extension registry.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Check redistribution terms for every bundled extension, including Copilot.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Retain applicable copyright and third-party notices.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] For a serious cross-platform product, the Arch package should be only one output of a common build
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] and release system—not the foundation of the product.
2026-09-22 08:59:33 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:22:58 [skid@archlinux] Account for Windows Defender/SmartScreen reputation.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gpt-5.6-sol 🌀 🪠 🧊 $0.042 27.28KB 9.37s
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] This means Windows may warn users when they download or run a new, uncommon installer—even when it
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] is harmless.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] Typical warning:
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 	icrosoft Defender SmartScreen prevented an unrecognized app from starting.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] SmartScreen considers factors such as the file’s digital signature, download prevalence, history,
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] and whether the file or signing identity is known to Microsoft.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] What to do
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Authenticode-sign every `.exe`, `.msi`, DLL, and installer with a trusted code-signing
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] certificate.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Keep the same certificate/signing identity across releases so reputation can accumulate.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Use stable filenames, publishers, domains, and download URLs.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Serve downloads over HTTPS.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Timestamp signatures so they remain valid after the certificate expires.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Avoid packers, obfuscators, unexpected PowerShell actions, and unnecessary privilege elevation.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Submit false detections or incorrectly blocked files through Microsoft’s security intelligence
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] submission portal.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Publish SHA-256 checksums so users can verify downloads.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Do not instruct ordinary users to disable Defender.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] Check an Authenticode signature from PowerShell:
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] Get-AuthenticodeSignature .\YourInstaller.exe
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] A newly issued certificate or low-download release may still initially receive “unrecognized app”
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] warnings. Signing proves the publisher and protects file integrity; it does not automatically
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] guarantee an established SmartScreen reputation.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] Also distinguish:
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Microsoft Defender Antivirus: scans for malware or suspicious behaviour.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Microsoft Defender SmartScreen: warns about unrecognized or low-reputation downloads and
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] applications.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Smart App Control: a separate Windows security feature that can enforce stricter trust
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] requirements.
2026-09-22 09:23:08 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
