2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] Backstory
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - The name originally meant KDE Non-Linear Video Editor.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Jason Wood started the project around 2002.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - It later became an official KDE project, maintained by community contributors.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - It is built with Qt and KDE Frameworks.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - Most media processing is provided by the MLT multimedia framework, which in turn uses
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] FFmpeg extensively.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] - It supports Linux, Windows, and macOS, although Linux remains its traditional platform.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] This layered design explains some of its rough edges: Kdenlive coordinates its own interface and
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] timeline with MLT, FFmpeg, effects, codecs, GPU/display systems, and desktop integration. Bugs can
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] arise at several of those boundaries.
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] On Arch, you can see the installed package details and licence with:
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] pacman -Qi kdenlive
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] The source is hosted under KDE’s infrastructure:
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] <https://invent.kde.org/multimedia/kdenlive>
2026-09-22 10:19:41 [gpt-5.6-sol] 
