2026-09-23 07:11:03 [skid@archlinux] size of cache?
2026-09-23 07:11:10 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.004 9.174KB 7.18s
2026-09-23 07:11:10 [gemini-3.8-flash] For a standard Pull Zone, Bunny.net does not expose a metric for the total volume of data currently
2026-09-23 07:11:10 [gemini-3.8-flash] stored in the edge cache.
2026-09-23 07:11:10 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:11:10 [gemini-3.8-flash] Because the edge cache is distributed across global Points of Presence (POPs) on volatile NVMe/RAM
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] drives and operates on a Least Recently Used (LRU) eviction model, there is no single aggregate
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] "cache size" value.
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] However, the Bunny.net Statistics API does provide cache volume and efficiency metrics across given
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] time windows:
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Cached Bandwidth: The total volume of bytes served directly out of the edge cache without
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] hitting your origin.
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Origin Bandwidth: The volume of bytes fetched from `https://skid.nz` when cache misses
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] occur.
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Cache Hit Rate: The percentage of total requests satisfied by the cache versus those
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] forwarded to the origin.
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] • (Note: If you were using a persistent Bunny Storage Zone rather than an external origin, the API
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] would report `StorageUsed` in bytes, but this does not apply to standard pull zones backed by a web
2026-09-23 07:11:11 [gemini-3.8-flash] server).*
