2026-09-23 07:12:06 [skid@archlinux] will data last for days, weeks?
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 gemini-3.8-flash 🌟 🪠 0.7° $0.006 10.58KB 5.54s
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] In practice, whether data remains cached for days or weeks depends on three primary factors:
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 1. Your Origin's Cache Headers
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] Because your Cache Max-Age Override is set to `-1s`, Bunny.net adheres strictly to the
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] headers sent by `https://skid.nz`:
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If your web server sends `Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000` (30 days), the edge nodes
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] consider the content fresh for up to 30 days.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If your origin sends short TTLs, `no-cache`, or omits expiration headers, files will expire
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] quickly or will not be cached at all.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 2. Request Frequency and LRU Eviction
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] Even with a high `max-age`, edge servers use Least Recently Used (LRU) eviction:
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Each global Point of Presence (POP) has finite high-speed storage.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • If an asset is not frequently requested through a specific POP, the edge server may evict it
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] after a few hours or days to free up capacity for higher-demand content.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • High-traffic files stay cached for the full duration of their TTL.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 3. Per-POP Caching
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] Each Bunny.net POP caches independently. A file requested by a visitor in Sydney is cached locally
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] in Sydney, but a subsequent visitor in London will trigger an origin fetch to populate the London
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] POP.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] Ensuring Multi-Week Retention
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] If you need assets to reliably stay cached for weeks regardless of request volume:
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] • Perma-Cache: Bunny.net offers a feature called Perma-Cache, which writes your
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] cached files to Bunny Storage nodes. This prevents LRU eviction on low-traffic files and serves all
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] POPs from the storage layer instead of querying your origin server.
2026-09-23 07:12:13 [gemini-3.8-flash] 
