2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 	this.instance.post([{
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 		command:"dig",
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 		outlines,
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 		depth:BasementDepth,
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 		border:40
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 	}]);
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] That is the only main-thread addition, and it is pure data marshalling — no geometry, no
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] rasterising, no surface building.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] Remove the main-thread dig
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] `Builder.buildTile`'s `build_roof2` block currently calls `tile.digOutline`. With the dig moved to
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] the worker it must not run again — the worker already zeroed `diff` and set `ground` before the
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] buffers were transferred. Delete that call (or the whole `build_roof2` block if you weren't using
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] the rest of it). Leaving it in would dig a second time on an already-transferred heightmap, which
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] is at best a no-op and at worst double-offsets `ground`.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] Ordering guarantees
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - The worker's two gates (`topoCount` and `digReady`) mean `createTopo` fires only when both the
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] merged heightmap and the outlines are present, regardless of which arrived first.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `postFlora` reads `diff`, which `digTopo` has already zeroed over each footprint, so building
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] cells fail `m.min>floraMin` and are omitted from the flora grid.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `post` transfers `topo`/`diff`/`ground` after both the dig and the flora pass, so the main thread
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] receives a single, final, consistent state — no rebuild in `meshTile`, no second flora pass, no
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] ordering assumptions on the main side.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] Small things
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `BasementDepth` is `4` in `wire_grid.js`. At that value the dig is invisible against the terrain.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] Bump it before you can judge the result — a few hundred is a reasonable starting point.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `Bits.poly` clamps `x` but not `y`; a negative `y` writes off the typed array. Roof outlines near
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] the tile edge will hit this. Worth fixing in `wire_util.js` before the worker starts relying on it.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `FloraPen` is `32`, which is outside `RoaPalette`'s 0–29 range. Set it to a real green (4, 9, 15,
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 24) — otherwise the flora you're now correctly generating will still render as whatever the driver
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] returns for an out-of-bounds uniform read.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] - `postFlora` writes `0,0,0` normals. `TopoFloraSurface` in `wire_core.js` does the same. Whichever
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] side ends up generating flora, `calcNormals` has to run on it before upload, or the surface stays
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] flat-lit regardless of the palette fix.
2026-09-27 23:32:38 [deepseek-flash] 
