2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] On 20
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] That's now in range, so you've fixed the out-of-bounds uniform read. Index 20 in `RoaPalette` is:
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] G,O,B,A    // (0.40, 0.94, 0.70) at alpha 0.52
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] Mint green, half transparent. Its opaque twin is index 9 (`G,O,B,O`), and a muted opaque green is
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] index 4 (`G,B,G,O`). If transparent is what you want, 20 is fine.
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] The dominant cause of darkness is still there
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] `worker_baker.js` `postFlora` still writes zero normals:
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] v.push([mx,my,mz,c, 0,0,0,0]);
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] //                 ^^^^^^^^^ nx,ny,nz
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] And nothing downstream computes them. `TopoTile.onFlora` just stores the surface:
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] onFlora(verts,indices){
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 	this.floraSurface=new Surface(verts,indices,[]);
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] `addTileShape` calls `addSurface`, not `addFlatSurface`, so it skips the `flatifyVerts →
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] calcNormals` path that `addFlatShape` takes. Result: the tile shader's `dot(normal, sun)` is zero
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] for every flora vertex, so the flora sits at ambient only. Palette index 20's alpha won't save it —
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] it'll still read as a dark mint silhouette.
