2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] // wire_topo.js onFlora
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] onFlora(verts,indices){
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 	this.floraSurface=new Surface(verts,indices,[]);
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 	const zfactor=4.6/(this.level*8.0);
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 	this.floraSurface.calcNormals(zfactor);
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] Same `zfactor` expression as `onBump`, so shading matches the terrain underneath. Do this first —
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] then you'll actually be judging the palette rather than the missing normals.
2026-09-28 10:38:15 [deepseek-flash] 
