2026-09-28 11:06:47 [skid@archlinux] logstats should include tiles in cache, if there is active distinction, also memory stats for all the layers
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.024 905.2KB 46.61s
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Yes — there's a distinction, but it's derived rather than stored, and one half of it leaks. That
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] matters because a stats report built on the leaky half will show a number that only ever grows.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] What "active" currently means
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Three separate notions exist, and they aren't the same set:
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] ╭───────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] │  Notion       │  Where                                      │  Meaning                                                                                                       │
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] ├───────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] │  **Touched**  │  `TopoTile.frame` vs `TopoGrid.frameCount`  │  Set by `touchTiles` for tiles that are `fetched && ready`; `sweep` removes them once `frame < frameCount-20`  │
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] │  **Meshed**   │  `GraphicsStack._activeTiles`               │  Pushed in `meshTile`; never removed                                                                           │
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] │  **Cached**   │  `TopoGrid._tileGrid`                       │  Everything in the grid, whether touched or not                                                                │
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] ╰───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] So "active vs cached" is `tile.frame >= frameCount-20` versus the rest of `_tileGrid`. That's
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] computable. But two things are broken around it:
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `GraphicsStack.flushTile` never splices `_activeTiles`. It removes the meshes from the
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] layers and calls `tile.retire()`, but the tile stays in the array. That array grows for the
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] lifetime of the session, so `_activeTiles.length` is a leak counter, not an active count.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `sweep` skips tiles whose `frame` was never set. The guard is `if(tile.frame &&
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] tile.frame<minFrame)`, and `undefined` is falsy, so a tile that was created by `tileGet` but never
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] touched — a failed load, or one created via `TopoGrid.pick` — is never swept and is retained
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] forever. Those are the real "cached" population.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Both are worth fixing before the number means anything.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Memory: what's reachable
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] The dominant cost is the heightmap, and it's fully reachable: `Bumpmap.topo/diff/ground` are
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] `Uint16Array(resres)`, so `3  res² * 2` bytes per tile. At `res=1024` that's 6.3 MB per
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] tile; a radius-5 view holds ~81 tiles, so ~500 MB. That dwarfs everything else.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Surfaces and shapes are reachable too, except GPU buffer sizes, which are computed in
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] `Shape.staticBuffer`/`instanceBuffer` and then discarded. Textures are counted in `SharedTextures`
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] but without dimensions. Both need a little bookkeeping to report honestly.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
