2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] // wire_graphics.js — GraphicsStack.flushTile
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] flushTile(tile){
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	const meesh=[tile.tilemesh,tile.floramesh,tile.staticmeesh,tile.flatmeesh].flat();
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	for(const mesh of meesh){
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 		if(mesh){
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 			const layer0=this.graphicsLayers[0];
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 			layer0.removeMesh(mesh);
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 		}
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	const active=this._activeTiles;
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	const index=active.indexOf(tile);
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	if(index>=0){
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 		active.splice(index,1);
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	tile.flushMesh();
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 	tile.retire();
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Without this, `activeTiles` in the report is meaningless. For the orphan set, the smallest safe
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] change is to stamp `tile.frame=this.frameCount` in `tileGet` so newly created tiles fall inside the
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] sweep window and are retired if nothing touches them — but check the fetch path first, since a slow
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] tile could then be swept while loading and re-created next frame.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Caveats on the numbers
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `orphan` is `cached` minus tiles that have at least been fetched, so it counts both failed loads
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] and `pick`-created tiles. If it climbs steadily, that's the `tileGet` leak.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `surfaceBytes` uses `tris.length * (vertCount>65535?4:2)` — a close match to the GL index buffer,
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] not the JS array's actual footprint.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `layerBytes` counts only what the `Shape` objects retain. Textures are counted globally in
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] `textures`, so a shape's texture cost isn't double-counted but also isn't attributed to its layer.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] - `topoTiles` levels with no tiles report zero, so an empty level is silent rather than absent —
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] worth showing, since it tells you the grid exists but hasn't fetched.
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] Want this folded into the design doc as a section, or submitted as a patch against the three files?
2026-09-28 11:07:34 [deepseek-flash] 
