2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Ordering in `createTopo`
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] The whole point. Dig, then flora, then post:
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] function createTopo(){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	const bytes=heightmaps[0]||[];
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	const heightmap=AllocBumpmap(bytes);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	heightmap.setBytes(bytes);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	const n=heightmaps.length;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	for(let i=1;i<n;i++){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		if(heightmaps[i].length==bytes.length){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			heightmap.orBytes(heightmaps[i]);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	heightmaps.length=0;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	for(const outline of roofOutlines){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		digOutline(heightmap,outline,digDepth,digBorder);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	roofOutlines.length=0;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	heightmap.postFlora(512,4,15,2);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	heightmap.post();
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] `digOutline` uses only `heightmap.pickTopo` and `heightmap.setGround/setHeight`, and the worker's
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] own `Bumpmap` implements all three — so the same free function works on both sides without
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] modification.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Getting `digOutline` into the worker
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Two options.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] • Option A — `importScripts`.* One line, but `wire_util.js` runs `const AppEventServer=new
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] EventServer();` at top level and `EventServer` constructs a `Worker` with a document-relative path.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Guard that line:
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] const AppEventServer=(typeof window!=="undefined")?new EventServer():null;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Then:
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] importScripts("../wirejs/wire_util.js");
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Path is relative to the worker's own URL (`.../nitrojs/worker_baker.js`), so `../wirejs/` is
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] correct.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] • Option B — inline `Bits` and `digOutline` into the worker.* Self-contained, no import,
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] but duplicates the rasteriser. Only worth it if you want the worker to stay dependency-free.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] I'd take A. The guard is one line and the worker stays in sync with the main-thread `Bits`.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Main thread — minimal
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] One helper, called from two places:
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] maybeSendDig(){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	if(this.digSent) return;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	if(this.drawingCount!=this.drawings.length) return;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	this.digSent=true;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	const outlines=[];
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	for(const drawing of this.drawings){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		for(const roof of drawing.data["ROOF"]){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			const start=roof.start;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			const count=roof.count;
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			for(let i=0;i<count;i++){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 				outlines.push(drawing.outlines[start+i]);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	if(this.instance){
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		this.instance.post([{
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			command:"dig",
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			outlines,
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			depth:BasementDepth,
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 			border:BasementBorder
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 		}]);
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Call it at the end of `onDrawingResponse` and at the end of `fetchTopoTile` (after the instance is
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] created). The second call covers `level>=3` and `UseLINZ=false`, where no drawing is fetched and
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] `digReady` would otherwise never be set.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Two decisions
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] • Fail-open or strict gate.* As written, if the drawing fetch errors out without calling
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] `onDrawingResponse`, the worker stalls forever — no bump, no flora, no tile. `hasLoaded()` already
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] stalls in that case on the main side, so it's not a new failure mode, but it does move the stall
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] into the worker. If you'd rather degrade, drop the `digReady` gate and instead send an empty `dig`
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] from a timer, or just let `createTopo` run when the topo is ready and dig only if outlines happen
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] to have arrived.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] • Shared border or two.* `BasementBorder=40` is the carve halo. Flora clearance wants to be
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] wider than the basement (eaves, not wall line). If they're different, `digTopo` needs either two
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] passes or a separate flora mask, which is a bigger change than a message.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] What still has to be true
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] - `BasementDepth` is `4`. At `SeaLevel=186*16` that's ~25 cm and won't read. Pick a value in those
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] units.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] - `build_roof2` in `Builder.buildTile` must not also call `tile.digOutline` — remove that call, or
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] the main thread digs a heightmap the worker already transferred and dug.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] - `Bits.poly` has the `y` clamp commented out. Worth a `bits.dump()` check before trusting edge
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] outlines, though `Bits` is allocated at the outline's own min so interior coordinates are
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] non-negative by construction.
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 11:36:24 [deepseek-flash] Want me to write this as the patch against `worker_baker.js`, `wire_util.js` and `wire_topo.js`?
