2026-09-28 12:36:14 [skid@archlinux] draw order of tiles is current issue
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.022 1.095MB 38.64s
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] Looking at the path, the order isn't chosen anywhere — it falls out of when a tile finishes
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] loading.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] How the order is actually determined
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `refreshTiles` hands tiles to `populateHome` in scan order:
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] for(let a=-r;a<=r;a++){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 	for(let b=-r;b<=r;b++){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 		if(a*a+b*b<=r*r){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 			const tile=this.tileGet(tx+a,ty+b);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 			if(tile.fetched){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 				if(tile.ready){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 					visible.push(tile);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] But `visible` only contains tiles that are `fetched && ready`, and tiles become ready
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] asynchronously. A tile is meshed on the first frame it appears there, and `meshTile` appends its
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] shapes to the layer:
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] tile.staticmeesh=layer0.addStaticShapes(surfaces,...);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] tile.tilemesh=layer0.addTileShape(topo,...);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `drawLayerList` then walks `layer.shapes` in that array order, so draw order == mesh order ==
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] order of load completion.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] And load order is nearest-first, because the fetch priority is a distance:
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] tile.priority=1-(a*a+b*b);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] this.fetchTile(tile);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `compareTiles` sorts ascending, `fetchTile` pops from the end, so the closest tile is fetched and
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] meshed first. The tile layer is therefore drawn front-to-back.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] Why that's visible
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] For an opaque, depth-tested scene, front-to-back is fine — it's even the fast path. It only bites
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] where geometry is blended or coincident:
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - Terrain alpha is `O=0.94`, and `WebGL2Context.clear` enables `BLEND` globally with depth writes
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] on. So each tile is 94% opaque and blended. Where adjacent tiles overlap at the seam, the second
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] tile blends over the first, and how much darkening you see depends on which was drawn first.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] Front-to-back makes it worse, and it changes as tiles stream in.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - Flora is genuinely transparent (`A=0.52`), so it needs strict back-to-front. Front-to-back
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] guarantees the wrong blend.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - Coincident surfaces (walls/coast on terrain) resolve by draw order because the depth func is
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `LESS`, not `LEQUAL`.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] Two ways out
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] • Make the opaque layers order-independent.* If the terrain is meant to be solid, alpha
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] should be `1.0` — the `0.94` is what forces blending and thus order sensitivity. That plus depth
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] test removes terrain from the problem entirely.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] • Sort the blended layer back-to-front each frame.* `populateHome` sorting at mesh time
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] won't hold, because a far tile that loads later still appends after the near ones. The sort has to
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] happen in the draw path, not the mesh path. Give each shape a depth key when it's created and order
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `layer.shapes` in `compileLayers`:
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] compileLayers(layers){
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 	this.layers=layers;
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 	this.drawlist=this.drawLayerList(layers);
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] `sortedShapes(layer)` there, sorting `shape.depth` descending, with `shape.depth` set from the
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] tile's position relative to `heading` in `addTileShape`.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] One thing to confirm first
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] Which symptom are you seeing?
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - Seams / dark lines between tiles → the `0.94` alpha, fix by making terrain opaque.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - A far tile painting over a near one → depth isn't doing its job (winding/culling, or
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] depth not written), not order.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] - Flora popping or blending wrong as you pan → the front-to-back mesh order, fix by sorting
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] in the draw path.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] The fix differs per case, so tell me which one and I'll write it against `wire_graphics.js` — I
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] don't have that file in this batch.
2026-09-28 12:36:55 [deepseek-flash] 
