2026-09-28 13:04:01 [skid@archlinux] for worker script do i need to make sure resources are not being leaked
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.019 1.105MB 28.83s
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Short answer: yes, but the risk isn't inside the worker — a `Worker` gets a fresh global scope and
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] is freed the moment you `terminate()` it. The risk is the main thread failing to terminate
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] it, plus main-side buffers that outlive the tile. The discipline is: every `TopoTile` must be
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] flushed exactly once, and nothing on the main thread may retain per-tile buffers.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Why the worker's own state is safe
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `heightmaps`, `roofOutlines`, `topoCount`, `digReady` are all module-level in `worker_baker.js`.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Each `new Worker(...)` is a separate global, so there's no cross-tile contamination, and
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `terminate()` discards the whole realm. `createTopo` also clears `heightmaps.length=0` and
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `roofOutlines.length=0`, and `post()` transfers `topo`/`diff`/`ground` out (detaching them). So the
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] worker holds nothing after a successful bake.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] The four real gaps
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] ╭─────┬──────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │  #  │  Leak                                    │  Cause                                                        │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] ├─────┼──────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │  1  │  Orphan workers                          │  sweep() only removes tiles with tile.frame set; tiles that   │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │     │                                          │  never became ready keep their Worker alive forever           │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │  2  │  Double instance                         │  fetchTopoTile() overwrites this.instance; only a debugger    │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │     │                                          │  guards it, so the old Worker leaks                           │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │  3  │  Main-thread heightmaps array            │  rawLoad() pushes raw and never clears; transfer is           │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │     │                                          │  commented out so the buffer is copied, not moved             │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] │  4  │  Worker holds heightmaps on stall        │  if createTopo never runs, heightmaps/roofOutlines never clear │
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] ╰─────┴──────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] • 1 — orphan workers.* `sweep()` uses `if(tile.frame && tile.frame<minFrame)`. `touchTiles`
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] only stamps `frame` on `fetched && ready` tiles, so anything that fetched but never finished is
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] never swept and its worker is never terminated. Stamp on creation so untouch-ed tiles age out:
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] tileGet(x,y){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	...
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	if(!tile){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		tile=new TopoTile(this,level,x,y);
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		tile.frame=this.frameCount;
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		grid[y][x]=tile;
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	return tile;
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Caveat: a tile mid-fetch now has a 20-frame window before it's swept and re-created. If fetches can
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] exceed that, sweep on `!fetched` instead, or raise the window.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] • 2 — double instance.* Make it explicit rather than a `debugger`:
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] if(this.hasBaker){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	if(this.instance){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		this.instance.terminate();
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		this.instance=null;
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	this.flushed=false;
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	this.instance=new TileInstance(this);
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	this.instance.bakeTopo(this.topoCount);
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] • 3 — main-thread buffer retention. `rawLoad` accumulates `raw` in `this.heightmaps`
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] and posts a copy* because the transfer is commented out. Neither is needed — the worker owns
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] the buffer:
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] rawLoad(raw){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	const message=[{command:"heightmap",array:raw}];
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	this.post(message,[raw.buffer]);
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Drop `this.heightmaps.push(raw)` entirely. `TileInstance.heightmaps` is only read by
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `TileInstance.createTopo`, which the baker path never calls — it's a dead accumulator. Same fix for
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `TileInstance.post` callers: pass the transfer.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] • 4 — worker retention on stall.* Covered by clearing in `createTopo`, but only if
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `createTopo` runs. See below.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] The thing that matters more than the leaks
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] As shipped, the worker gate will never open. `refresh()` is:
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] function refresh(){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady){
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 		createTopo();
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `digReady` is `false` until `onDig` fires, and I can't find a `dig` post anywhere on the main side
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] — `onDrawingResponse` still ends at `this.drawings.push(drawing)`. So `createTopo` never runs: no
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] bump, no flora, no mesh, and `heightmaps`/`roofOutlines` grow for the life of every worker. That's
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] leak #1 and #4 at once, and it presents as an empty view, not as a memory problem.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] You need `maybeSendDig()` wired into `onDrawingResponse` and the end of `fetchTopoTile`
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] (the second call covers `level>=3`, where no drawing is fetched and nothing would ever set
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] `digReady`).
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] Summary
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] - Worker realm itself: no leak, terminate = freed.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] - Terminate discipline: fix the orphan sweep and the double-instance overwrite.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] - Main thread: stop retaining `raw` buffers; transfer them.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] - Blocker: without the main-thread `dig` send, every worker stalls and retains everything. Fix that
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] first — it's both the render bug and the biggest leak.
2026-09-28 13:04:30 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪣 0.7° $0.025 1.277MB 44.15s
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] Read the batch against the previous versions. Several real changes, and two of them mean the dig
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] feature is currently inert. Details below.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 1. Duplicate `refresh()` — the dig gate is dead
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] `worker_baker.js` now declares `refresh` twice:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] function refresh(){
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady){	// first
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 		createTopo();
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] ...
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] function refresh(){
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 	if(topoCount==heightmaps.length){				// second, later in file
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 		createTopo();
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 	}
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] Function declarations hoist and the last one wins. So the live `refresh` is the ungated
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] version: `digReady` is never consulted, `onDig` is never required, and `createTopo` fires on the
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] topo count alone.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] That's actually why tiles still load. If you delete the second declaration and keep the gated one,
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] tiles will hang forever, because the main thread never sends `dig` (no `maybeSendDig` in
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] `wire_topo.js`). So the duplicate is masking a missing sender. Decide which way you want it:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] - Keep it simple for now: delete the first (gated) declaration, accept no dig, and wire `dig`
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] later.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] - Or wire the sender and delete the second.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] Right now `digReady` is a dead variable and `createTopo`'s `digReady=true;` does nothing.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 2. `digOutline` is undefined in the worker
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] `createTopo` calls it:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] for(const outline of roofOutlines){
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 	digOutline(heightmap,outline,digDepth,digBorder);
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] But `worker_baker.js` has no `digOutline`, no `Bits`, and no `importScripts`. It only survives
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] because `roofOutlines` is always empty. The moment a `dig` message lands, that's a `ReferenceError`
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] and the worker dies silently (no `onerror` handler), so the tile never meshes.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] Also `//	roofOutlines.length=0;` is commented out, so if `createTopo` ever ran twice the same
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] outlines would be re-dug.
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 3. Flora: two generators, and the main one is broken
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] `meshTile` now builds its own flora and ignores the worker's:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] const floraSurface=TopoFloraSurface(256,8,0,tile.heightmap);
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] const floramesh=layer0.addTileShape(floraSurface,tile.basemap,tile.scratch,origin);
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] Two problems in that one call:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] • Missing `floraMin`.* Signature is `TopoFloraSurface(count,mag,c,topo,floraMin)`. You pass
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] four args, so `floraMin` is `undefined`. Inside:
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] if(m.min>floraMin){		// number > undefined → NaN compare → always false
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:18:09 [deepseek-flash] 
