2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.021 1.422MB 22.23s
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] Order doesn't matter to the worker. The gate is `topoCount==heightmaps.length && digReady`, so the
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] outlines can arrive before or after the topo, and `createTopo` fires when the last of the two
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] lands. Sending early is safe — the worker just holds the outlines.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] What matters on the main thread is completeness: send once, when you have the whole outline
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] set for the tile.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] The condition
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] if(this.digSent) return;
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] if(this.drawingCount!=this.drawings.length) return;
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] this.digSent=true;
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `drawingCount` is incremented at request time in `fetchDrawing`, `drawings.length` at response time
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] in `onDrawingResponse`. So `drawingCount == drawings.length` is true only once every requested
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] drawing has responded — including the error path, which also calls `onDrawingResponse`.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] Two call sites, both needed
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] - End of `onDrawingResponse` — the normal path.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] - End of `fetchTopoTile`, after the instance is created — the zero-drawings path. Covers
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `level>=3`, `UseLINZ=false`, and tiles with no `roa` layer in range. Without this, `digReady` never
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] becomes true and the worker stalls forever: no bump, no flora, no tile.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] The two are mutually exclusive given the completeness check. At the end of `fetchTopoTile`, if
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] drawings were requested then `drawingCount>0` and `drawings.length==0`, so it skips;
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `onDrawingResponse` sends later. If none were requested, `0==0` and it sends an empty list;
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `onDrawingResponse` never fires.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] The instance
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `this.instance` is guaranteed to exist by the time either site runs. `fetchTopoTile` creates it
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] synchronously at the end of its source loop, and `fetchDrawing`'s `.then` callbacks are queued
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] behind that synchronous body. So no check needed — but if you'd rather be defensive,
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `if(this.instance)` costs nothing.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] The guard
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `digSent` is not strictly required — the completeness check already fires exactly once per request
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] cycle. Keep it anyway: it makes the intent explicit, and it survives someone later adding a third
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] call site.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] One thing to fix alongside
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `// roofOutlines.length=0;` in `createTopo` is still commented out. After the first run,
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] `heightmaps.length` is 0 so `refresh` won't re-fire `createTopo`, which means a stray second `dig`
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] won't corrupt the transfer — but the outlines accumulate in the worker for the life of the
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] instance. Uncomment it.
2026-09-29 13:28:00 [deepseek-flash] 
