2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] But it also means the dig path is now fully dead: `createTopo` fires on the topo count alone, so
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] any `dig` message that arrives later finds `roofOutlines` populated but `createTopo` already run.
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] The gate only does something if `digReady` starts `false` and the message arrives before the topo
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] completes.
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] If you're keeping this for now, fine — just be aware the `dig` case in `onmessage`, `onDig`, and
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] the `roofOutlines` loop are all currently no-ops.
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] `wire_topo.js` — `TileInstance.digTopo()` is broken and never called
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:41:00 [deepseek-flash] 
