2026-09-29 19:43:46 [skid@archlinux] current situation is buildings are fixed height while i position them so they stick to ground,
2026-09-29 19:44:15 [skid@archlinux] the gap between building and ground varies so maybe scalar is in effect for terrain?
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.4 deepseek-flash 🐋 🪠 0.7° $0.030 1.549MB 45.07s
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] No — there's no separate scalar on terrain z. Terrain and wall vertices are both raw topo units,
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] both offset by the same origin (`0x4000`), both pushed through the same `RawView` matrix. So the
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] mismatch isn't a scale.
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:00 [deepseek-flash] Three real causes, in order of how much they'd move a wall base.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 1. Terrain uses a 9-sample minimum; walls use a single sample
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] Terrain z, from `CreateTopoSurface`:
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] const z=ground||minz;   // minz = pickTopo(...).min, min of 9 elevations
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] v.push([mx,my,z,c, 0,0,0,bits]);
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] Wall base z, from `walledSpiral`:
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] const g0=topo.pickElevation(px,py);   // single sample
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] verts.push([px,-py,g0,pu,0,0,0,wallc]);
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `pickTopo` samples at ±`factor*8` in index space; `pickElevation` samples once. On any relief, the
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 9-sample min sits below the single sample, and the difference is exactly the local relief.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] Flat ground → no gap. Slope or edge → gap. That's your "varies".
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] The window is resolution-dependent: ±2 px at `res=1024`, ±8 px at `res=2048` (`m=factor*8`, then
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `index` multiplies by `factor` again). So the gap also changes with tile resolution.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 2. Missing data became a deep pit
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `worker_baker.js setBytes` now does:
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] }else{
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash]     topo[i]=TopoNoLevel;   // -0x4000
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] and `heal()` is not called in `createTopo`. Any pixel where `h==0` (LiDAR hole, water mask, swath
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] edge) is now −16384 units. `pickTopo` samples 9 points, so a single hole in the window pulls `minz`
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] to −16384 and the terrain vertex spikes down. That reads as wildly variable terrain around
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] buildings — much larger than the ±4–8 unit sampling effect above.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] The old code left those as `0`, which was a benign sea-level-ish value. If you want holes visible,
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] that's a deliberate change; if not, `heal()` or clamp `minz` when any sample is `TopoNoLevel`.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 3. The fixed top is 100 m
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] const h1=+1600;
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] verts.push([px,-py,h0+h1,pu,0,0,0,wallc]);
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `SeaLevel=186*16` implies 16 units/m, so `1600` = 100 m. The previous line was
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `sampleHeight(px,py,2).max + 16`, i.e. tracked the detail channel. If you want the wall to look
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] grounded, the top value is separate from the base gap — but a 100 m wall will read wrong regardless
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] of where the base sits.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] What amplifies all of it
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `refreshGraphics` sets `hfac=0.77/hshift` with `hshift=1<<(level3)`, and
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `TranslateZoomAngleAspect` uses `zoomz=zoomhfac/512`. So z is exaggerated 8× more at level
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 1 than at level 2. Terrain and walls scale together — it's not a mismatch — but any base gap
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] you fix at level 2 will look 8× worse at level 1.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] To close the gap
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] Pick one, in increasing order of effort:
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] - Match the sampling. Make the wall base `topo.pickTopo(px,py).min` instead of
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `pickElevation`. Cheapest, directly cancels cause 1.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] - Sink the base. `pickTopo(px,py).min - 64` (or whatever margin reads well). Robust to
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] future changes in terrain sampling.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] - Fix the holes. Restore `heal()` in `createTopo`, or clamp in `pickTopo`:
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash]   if(h0===TopoNoLevel) h0=h4;   // fall back to centre sample
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash]   for each of the nine, before taking min. Without this, causes 1 and 3 don't matter — the pit
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] dominates.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] - Reconsider `+1600`. If buildings should have varying height, drive it from
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] `sampleHeight(...).max` or from the drawing's storey attribute, not a constant.
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] If after fixing 1 and 2 you still see a residual gap that scales with view level, that's `hfac` and
2026-09-29 19:45:01 [deepseek-flash] it's expected — both surfaces move together, so it's a look, not a bug.
