2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Current order, derived from the code:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] What sets it
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] `drawLayerList` walks `layer.shapes` in array order. `addShape` pushes. So tile draw order == mesh
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] order.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] `meshTile` runs from `populateHome(visibleTiles, ...)`, and `visibleTiles` is built in
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] `refreshTiles`:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] for(let a=-r;a<=r;a++){
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	for(let b=-r;b<=r;b++){
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 		if(a*a+b*b<=r*r){
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 			const tile=this.tileGet(tx+a,ty+b);
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 			if(tile.fetched){
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 				if(tile.ready){ visible.push(tile); }
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Two filters stack:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - Scan order — `a` outer, `b` inner.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - Readiness — only `fetched && ready` tiles land in `visible`.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] So the array is scan-ordered within a frame, but a tile only enters on the frame it becomes
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] ready. A far tile that loads late appends after near ones. Across frames the order is effectively
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] load-completion order, which is nearest-first because of the fetch priority:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] tile.priority=1-(a*a+b*b);   // closest = highest
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] this.fetchList.sort(compareTiles);   // ascending
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] this.fetchList.pop();                 // takes highest
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Net: roughly front-to-back, but not guaranteed. Not a design decision, a consequence.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Does it matter
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] The `tile` layer is tagged `depthEnable`, so it's depth-tested with `LESS`, and `depthMask` is
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] default true. Terrain tiles are disjoint in world xy — each covers its own 2048² area. So for the
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] terrain itself, order is irrelevant; the depth buffer resolves it, and front-to-back is the cheap
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] path anyway.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Where order does bite:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - Blend. `WebGL2Context.clear` enables `BLEND` globally and never disables it. Terrain
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] alpha is `0.94` (`O` in `RoaPalette`), flora is `0.52` (`A`). Blended geometry needs back-to-front.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Front-to-back gives the wrong blend wherever two blended fragments cover the same pixel.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - Equal z. Depth func is `LESS`, not `LEQUAL`. Two surfaces at exactly the same z resolve
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] by draw order — first one drawn wins.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - `depthDisable` pass. Lines and sprites are drawn before everything, with no depth
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] test. Pure draw order, no z-buffer safety net.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] If your symptom is "a far tile draws over a near one", that isn't order — depth test would prevent
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] it. That'd be winding/culling, or depth not written. If your symptom is seams or flora blending
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] wrong, it is order.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] If you want back-to-front
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] The sort has to live in the draw path, not `meshTile`, because the `shapes` array persists across
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] frames and only changes on mesh/flush. Sort in `drawLayerList`, using each shape's origin from
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] `transforms[0]`:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] function sortShapes(shapes,m){
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	const a=m[4];
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	const b=m[5];
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	const keyed=shapes.map((shape,index)=>{
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 		const t=shape.transforms[0];
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 		return {shape,depth:a*t[3]+b*t[7],index};
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	});
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	keyed.sort((p,q)=>p.depth-q.depth);
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 	return keyed.map(k=>k.shape);
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] }
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] `t[3],t[7]` are the origin xy set by `setOrigin`. `m[4],m[5]` are the view matrix's xy→screen-y
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] terms, so the dot product is proportional to screen y; NDC +y is up-screen, which is back.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Ascending sort draws back first.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] Two notes:
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - Sort only the blended layers. `static` and `tile` are mostly opaque and depth-tested;
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] reordering them buys nothing but costs the sort every frame.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] - `z_clip` is pure world z. Row 2 of the matrix is `[0, 0, -1/2048, 0.5]`. So the depth
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] buffer already orders correctly by height, independent of draw order. Sorting only affects what
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] depth can't separate.
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] 
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] What are you actually seeing — tiles overpainting each other, seams, or something in the flora? The
2026-09-29 20:32:11 [deepseek-flash] fix differs.
